{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10957,10992p;11083,11143p;11573,11593p;11721,11786p'; ls -a docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers\"","aggregated_output":" 10957\t## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n 10958\t\n 10959\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n 10960\t  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n 10961\t  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n 10962\t- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n 10963\t  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n 10964\t  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n 10965\t  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n 10966\t- **Diagnosis:**\n 10967\t  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n 10968\t     figures.\n 10969\t  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n 10970\t  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n 10971\t  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n 10972\t- **Measured:**\n 10973\t  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n 10974\t  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n 10975\t  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n 10976\t  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n 10977\t  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n 10978\t- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n 10979\t  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n 10980\t  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n 10981\t  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n 10982\t    reference);\n 10983\t  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n 10984\t  - extraction unchanged;\n 10985\t  - families declared for the test.\n 10986\t- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n 10987\t- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n 10988\t  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n 10989\t- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n 10990\t\n 10991\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n 10992\t\n 11083\t## D731 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid-gate harness is ready to send (council round 47h); the first attempt is scored on both arms; the ceiling is Alex's\n 11084\t\n 11085\t- **What was built (D730):** `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py` (plan, send, recover, packets, verdict, replay),\n 11086\t  `paid_rehearsal.py` (the provider stubbed at urllib beneath the real budget transport), `paid_mutants.py`; the plan is pinned\n 11087\t  (`paid-plan.sha256`, 6f81dae5…). Record: `PAID-GATE.md` §3 to §3h.\n 11088\t- **Council rounds 47 to 47h** (Codex thread `01a20501…`, read-only): each round's findings were checked against the code and fixed\n 11089\t  with a rehearsal case and a mutant; round 47h answered \"READY TO SEND (once Alex names the ceiling)\".\n 11090\t- **Decided by the council (D725's lines unchanged):**\n 11091\t  - The first attempt is scored on both arms. D725 registers the arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about\n 11092\t    retries. A joint retry can repair a cross-card conflict that the separate arm sees only after both calls end, so scoring the\n 11093\t    final answers would credit the joint arm with a second chance the separate arm cannot have. Retries are sent after every first\n 11094\t    attempt and read for diagnosis only (`attempts.md`, `retries.jsonl`).\n 11095\t  - The readers' packets hold only what their four questions need, per card the scored answer's passages, figures, recomputed\n 11096\t    outcome, assumptions and card. No attempt history, code decision or check code (a cross-member code would reveal the arm).\n 11097\t  - The text the readers receive commits to the packet-to-unit mapping: a salted key's sha256 is its first line. The verdict renders\n 11098\t    every packet again from the run and refuses any mismatch.\n 11099\t  - The separate arm's two answers are reconciled one to one: a declared shared forecast is unified only when each call holds exactly\n 11100\t    one, with the same value, bounds and unit.\n 11101\t  - Completeness is judged on the scored attempts. The readings are sealed into the run, the verdict is written once, and `replay`\n 11102\t    must reproduce it.\n 11103\t- **Checks:** rehearsal 63 of 63 (three runs); mutants 33 of 33 caught, the control passes; the $0 gate unchanged (87 of 87, gate run 27).\n 11104\t- **Cost, at `hivemind.model.PRICES` (gpt-6-luna $0.10 input, $0.50 output per million tokens; tokens estimated as characters / 4):**\n 11105\t  - the 36 first attempts are about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n 11106\t  - the budget transport reserves at most $0.039 for one request before sending;\n 11107\t  - so $0.50 covers every scored attempt. Retries come last, and a ceiling stop among them leaves the scored test complete.\n 11108\t- **Next:** Alex names the ceiling (proposed $0.50). Nothing has been sent.\n 11109\t\n 11110\t## D732 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the paid gate's ceiling is $0.50\n 11111\t\n 11112\t- **The question** (after D731): \"judging-v13 花钱那一关（36 次计分请求，按公开价格约 0.17 美元，最坏 0.39 美元；重试排在最后、只作诊断）已经过理事会，现在可以发。你给多少上限？\"\n 11113\t  Options:\n 11114\t  - 0.5 美元 (recommended);\n 11115\t  - 0.8 美元;\n 11116\t  - 先不发.\n 11117\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\".\n 11118\t- **Decided (Alex):** `paid_gate.py`'s `APPROVED_CEILING` is 0.5. The gate is sent once, from an empty folder\n 11119\t  (`poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`), detached with a log and pid file, after a machine and network check. It is scored by\n 11120\t  `PAID-GATE.md` §4 on the first attempts.\n 11121\t\n 11122\t## D733 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid gate: STOP, every answer refused; the format's rules were never stated in the request (council round 48); repair or close is Alex's choice\n 11123\t\n 11124\t- **What ran** (D732): 36 scored first attempts and 36 diagnostic retries, gpt-6-luna, $0.3677 of $0.50 (ledger: 72 attempts,\n 11125\t  not stopped). Run folder `poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`. Record: `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`.\n 11126\t- **Registered result (D725's lines, scored as written, D680):** all 72 answers refused by `calc_check.py`, none published; the joint\n 11127\t  arm is usable in 0 of 9 pairs (needs 8). **STOP.** Complete, not INCOMPLETE: every attempt finished. The blind reading was not run:\n 11128\t  its brief says a card with no answer cannot be usable, and every card has none.\n 11129\t- **What it measures:** not D725's question (whether one call over a family gives better numbers), only that the answer format, as\n 11130\t  the request stated it, could not be filled.\n 11131\t- **Census (council round 48; Codex reproduced every refusal):**\n 11132\t  - 0 of 90 member answers named a figure as the outcome; the model wrote the number in words (\"$398.1 billion\");\n 11133\t  - prose where an id is expected, first attempts: `reference.figure` 39, `evidence` 175 (139 on source figures), `bridge` 49;\n 11134\t  - 52 figures gave both a value and a range;\n 11135\t  - the structure check stopped 63 of 72 answers before any source or arithmetic check.\n 11136\t- **Mechanism:**\n 11137\t  - The format's rules live in the check, not in the request. The sent schema has 7 field descriptions. `evidence`, `outcome`,\n 11138\t    `unit`, `value`/`low`/`high`, `inputs`, `operation`, `signs` and ten more have none.\n 11139\t  - The descriptions of `bridge` and `reference` read as asking for prose, while the check reads ids.\n 11140\t  - Under that layer, checks refuse right answers:\n 11141\t    - Q1 + Q2 = \"first half\" is refused (the parser reads only `H1`);\n 11142\t    - a source-stated year-over-year growth applied to last year's quarter needs a bridge;\n 11143\t    - $411 billion × 92.5% is computed by `product` as 38,017.5;\n 11573\t## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n 11574\t\n 11575\t- **The question** (after D746): \"资料没直接给出题目问的那个数，只能拿一个相关的数字来比。比如问四大云厂商今年的数据中心开支能不能过 7000 亿，资料只说“这四家 AI 基础设施开支超过 7300 亿”。这种比较能说明结果更可能落在线的某一边，但另一边也还有可能。这时系统可以发布预测吗，还是要等资料能直接算出落在哪边？\"\n 11576\t  - Options:\n 11577\t    - \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\": the answer must explain why the comparison applies to the companies, the year and the quantity\n 11578\t      asked, and why, under its own assumptions, that side is more likely; an answer that cannot explain it is not supported;\n 11579\t    - \"先说“还判断不了”\";\n 11580\t    - \"先停在这里\".\n 11581\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\".\n 11582\t- **Decided (Alex).** When the passages do not give the asked quantity, a forecast may rest on a related figure. It is supported\n 11583\t  only when the answer explains two things: why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked; and why,\n 11584\t  under the answer's own stated assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely. An answer that cannot explain this is not\n 11585\t  supported.\n 11586\t  - D741 ruling 3 still holds: a total used for a narrower quantity states the deduction as its own figure, or gives a supported\n 11587\t    bound.\n 11588\t  - D745's ruling still holds: a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n 11589\t- **Next (D746).** The ruling's words go into the shared reader definitions (`blind_rules.py`). Then one $0 blinded re-read of nine\n 11590\t  stored answers, registered with its expected readings and reviewed by the council before any packet is read.\n 11591\t\n 11592\t## D748 · 2026-11-23 · The D747 re-read fails on a self-contradicting floor; three of four earlier splits settle under the ruling; council 63: ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair; the paid re-send stays on hold\n 11593\t\n 11721\t## D752 · 2026-11-23 · D751 fails, so the wording loop ends under its exit rule; council 69–69b: two questions to Alex (the E-type publication default, agreed; the paid re-send, split)\n 11722\t\n 11723\t- **The D751 result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md`): FAIL on one settled line.\n 11724\t  - X01, E Claude, $37B: the 85% growth was an interpolation between the market pace and \"more than double\"; no passage sizes a\n 11725\t    shortfall.\n 11726\t  - Passed:\n 11727\t    - E Codex: a justified \"can't tell\", for the third run in a row;\n 11728\t    - S Codex: supported;\n 11729\t    - both P-v8 forecasts: supported;\n 11730\t    - both controls: caught.\n 11731\t  - Split: S Claude's $20B deduction.\n 11732\t- **The record across the five runs** (`BLIND7-RESULT.md` §2):\n 11733\t  - The Codex writer invented cuts twice, then gave three justified \"can't tell\" answers on E, each accepted by both families.\n 11734\t  - The Claude writer's five E forecasts never earned settled support (four settled no, one split).\n 11735\t  - P-v8 was supported in every run, and the controls were caught 6 of 6 since D749. S is mixed.\n 11736\t  - Only the paid gate compares joint against reconciled separate pairs, D725's hypothesis. No free test can answer it.\n 11737\t- **The exit rule fired** (council 67, registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D751]). The wording loop ends, and the publication choice\n 11738\t  for E-type cases returns to Alex.\n 11739\t- **Council round 69** (`codex-r69.md`) and **69b** (`codex-r69b.md`):\n 11740\t  - **Agreed, question 1.** When a reaffirmed target sits near a band line and, after weighing it with the other evidence, neither\n 11741\t    band is more likely, the recommended default is \"can't tell yet\", naming the fact that would decide it. It needs no request\n 11742\t    change, because line 9 already states it and Alex endorsed it (D745, D749). The alternative, the target's band by default, would\n 11743\t    be a new publication policy.\n 11744\t  - **Split, question 2.**\n 11745\t    - Codex recommends keeping the paid re-send on hold, because Alex made a clean free pass the condition and D751 failed.\n 11746\t    - Claude recommends a one-time exception, because only the paid run measures luna and the joint-against-separate comparison,\n 11747\t      within Alex's own $0.50 cap. Under the gate's lines, an E-type failure by luna would show as STOP rather than hide.\n 11748\t    - Both agree the exception must be presented with its case. The 36 scored requests and any diagnostic retries share the $0.50\n 11749\t      cap, and a pass earns design work only.\n 11750\t  - **Claude's overstatement, corrected.** \"The Claude writer failed five times\" became \"none of five forecasts earned settled\n 11751\t    support; one split\".\n 11752\t- **Pending:** Alex's answers to the two questions. Under D439 nothing paid is started.\n 11753\t\n 11754\t## D753 · 2026-11-23 · Alex chooses \"can't tell yet\" as the E-type default and a one-time paid exception\n 11755\t\n 11756\t- **The questions** (after D752):\n 11757\t  1. \"公司重申一个目标，正好落在两个预测档之间的那条线附近（比如 Vera CPU 明年“超过翻倍”，正好压在 400 亿线上）。把目标和其他证据都权衡过，还是说不出哪一档更可能。这时系统应该给读者看什么？\" Options:\n 11758\t     - \"显示“暂时判断不了” (推荐)\": the target as context, \"can't tell yet\", and the missing fact named; the council agreed; no\n 11759\t       request change;\n 11760\t     - \"按公司目标所在的档\".\n 11761\t  2. \"最后一次不花钱的写手测试里，有一份 E 题预测被两家都判了没依据，没达到你定的“0 元测试干净通过才付费”。理事会在这一题上意见不一：Codex 主张先不付费，我主张破例一次。你选哪个？\" Options:\n 11762\t     - \"先不付费，停在这里\" (Codex);\n 11763\t     - \"破例一次，付费重发\" (Claude): 36 requests to luna, ≤ $0.50 including retries; a pass earns design work only, and an E-type\n 11764\t       forced number stops the run;\n 11765\t     - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n 11766\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23): \"显示“暂时判断不了” (推荐)\"; \"破例一次，付费重发\".\n 11767\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11768\t  1. When a reaffirmed target sits near a band line and, after weighing it with the other evidence, neither band is more likely, the\n 11769\t     system shows \"can't tell yet\" with the target as context and names the deciding fact. The request already states it (line 9);\n 11770\t     nothing changes.\n 11771\t  2. A one-time exception to D749's clean-pass condition: the paid re-send of the 36 requests, rebuilt in v13s with the D751 request,\n 11772\t     under D725's lines and the paid gate's reading rule (`PAID-GATE.md` §4), with a total cap of $0.50 including diagnostic\n 11773\t     retries. It is prepared at $0 and reviewed by the council before the send.\n.\n..\nBLIND-RESULT.md\nBLIND2-RESULT.md\nBLIND3-RESULT.md\nBLIND4-RESULT.md\nBLIND5-RESULT.md\nBLIND6-RESULT.md\nBLIND7-RESULT.md\nDESIGN.md\nGATE-RESULT.md\nPAID-GATE-RESULT.md\nPAID-GATE.md\nPAPER-CHECK-D751.md\nREPAIR-DESIGN.md\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md\nRESULT.md\nSMALL-DESIGN.md\n__pycache__\nassemble_readings.py\nblind4.py\nblind5.py\nblind6.py\nblind7.py\nblind_adjudicate.py\nblind_reread.py\nblind_reread2.py\nblind_rules.py\nblind_test.py\ncalc_check.py\ncalc_small.py\nclaude-r45.md\nclaude-r48.md\nclaude-r49.md\nclaude-r56.md\nclaude-r57.md\nclaude-r58.md\nclaude-r59.md\nclaude-r61.md\nclaude-r63.md\nclaude-r65.md\nclaude-r67.md\ncodex-r45.md\ncodex-r45.stream\ncodex-r45b.md\ncodex-r45b.stream\ncodex-r46.md\ncodex-r46.stream\ncodex-r46aa.md\ncodex-r46aa.stream\ncodex-r46ab.md\ncodex-r46ab.stream\ncodex-r46ac.md\ncodex-r46ac.stream\ncodex-r46ad.md\ncodex-r46ad.stream\ncodex-r46b.md\ncodex-r46b.stream\ncodex-r46c.md\ncodex-r46c.stream\ncodex-r46d.md\ncodex-r46d.stream\ncodex-r46e.md\ncodex-r46e.stream\ncodex-r46f.md\ncodex-r46f.stream\ncodex-r46g.md\ncodex-r46g.stream\ncodex-r46h.md\ncodex-r46h.stream\ncodex-r46i.md\ncodex-r46i.stream\ncodex-r46j.md\ncodex-r46j.stream\ncodex-r46k.md\ncodex-r46k.stream\ncodex-r46l.md\ncodex-r46l.stream\ncodex-r46m.md\ncodex-r46m.stream\ncodex-r46n.md\ncodex-r46n.stream\ncodex-r46o.md\ncodex-r46o.stream\ncodex-r46p.md\ncodex-r46p.stream\ncodex-r46q.md\ncodex-r46q.stream\ncodex-r46r.md\ncodex-r46r.stream\ncodex-r46s.md\ncodex-r46s.stream\ncodex-r46t.md\ncodex-r46t.stream\ncodex-r46u.md\ncodex-r46u.stream\ncodex-r46v.md\ncodex-r46v.stream\ncodex-r46w.md\ncodex-r46w.stream\ncodex-r46x.md\ncodex-r46x.stream\ncodex-r46y.md\ncodex-r46y.stream\ncodex-r46z.md\ncodex-r46z.stream\ncodex-r47.md\ncodex-r47.stream\ncodex-r47b.md\ncodex-r47b.stream\ncodex-r47c.md\ncodex-r47c.stream\ncodex-r47d.md\ncodex-r47d.stream\ncodex-r47e.md\ncodex-r47e.stream\ncodex-r47f.md\ncodex-r47f.stream\ncodex-r47g.md\ncodex-r47g.stream\ncodex-r47h.md\ncodex-r47h.stream\ncodex-r48.md\ncodex-r48.stream\ncodex-r49.md\ncodex-r49.stream\ncodex-r50.md\ncodex-r50.stream\ncodex-r51.md\ncodex-r51.stream\ncodex-r52.md\ncodex-r52.stream\ncodex-r53.md\ncodex-r53.stream\ncodex-r54.md\ncodex-r54.stream\ncodex-r55.md\ncodex-r55.stream\ncodex-r56.md\ncodex-r56.stream\ncodex-r56b.md\ncodex-r56b.stream\ncodex-r56c.md\ncodex-r56c.stream\ncodex-r57.md\ncodex-r57.stream\ncodex-r58.md\ncodex-r58.stream\ncodex-r59.md\ncodex-r59.stream\ncodex-r60.md\ncodex-r60.stream\ncodex-r61.md\ncodex-r61.stream\ncodex-r61b.md\ncodex-r61b.stream\ncodex-r62.md\ncodex-r62.stream\ncodex-r63.md\ncodex-r63.stream\ncodex-r64.md\ncodex-r64.stream\ncodex-r65.md\ncodex-r65.stream\ncodex-r66.md\ncodex-r66.stream\ncodex-r67.md\ncodex-r67.stream\ncodex-r68.md\ncodex-r68.stream\ncodex-r69.md\ncodex-r69.stream\ncodex-r69b.md\ncodex-r69b.stream\ncodex-r70.md\ncodex-r70.stream\ngate-run1.txt\ngate-run10.fixtures.json\ngate-run10.txt\ngate-run11.fixtures.json\ngate-run11.txt\ngate-run12.fixtures.json\ngate-run12.txt\ngate-run13.fixtures.json\ngate-run13.txt\ngate-run14.fixtures.json\ngate-run14.txt\ngate-run15.fixtures.json\ngate-run15.txt\ngate-run16.fixtures.json\ngate-run16.txt\ngate-run17.fixtures.json\ngate-run17.txt\ngate-run18.fixtures.json\ngate-run18.txt\ngate-run19.fixtures.json\ngate-run19.txt\ngate-run2.txt\ngate-run20.fixtures.json\ngate-run20.txt\ngate-run21.fixtures.json\ngate-run21.txt\ngate-run22.fixtures.json\ngate-run22.txt\ngate-run23.fixtures.json\ngate-run23.txt\ngate-run24.fixtures.json\ngate-run24.txt\ngate-run25.fixtures.json\ngate-run25.txt\ngate-run26.fixtures.json\ngate-run26.txt\ngate-run27.fixtures.json\ngate-run27.txt\ngate-run3.fixtures.json\ngate-run3.txt\ngate-run4.fixtures.json\ngate-run4.txt\ngate-run5.fixtures.json\ngate-run5.txt\ngate-run6.fixtures.json\ngate-run6.txt\ngate-run7.fixtures.json\ngate-run7.txt\ngate-run8.fixtures.json\ngate-run8.txt\ngate-run9.fixtures.json\ngate-run9.txt\ngate.py\njudging-v13-draft.txt\njudging-v13s-d745.txt\njudging-v13s-d749.txt\njudging-v13s-d750.txt\njudging-v13s.txt\nmutants.log\nmutants.py\npaid-mutants.log\npaid-plan-v13s.json\npaid-plan-v13s.sha256\npaid-plan.json\npaid-plan.sha256\npaid_gate.py\npaid_mutants.py\npaid_rehearsal.py\nr56b\nreader-brief-v13.md\nrehearsal.log\nrender-r1.answer.json\nrender-r1.request.json\nrender-r1.txt\nrender_v13.py\nround45-brief.md\nround45b-brief.md\nround46-brief.md\nround46aa-brief.md\nround46ab-brief.md\nround46ac-brief.md\nround46ad-brief.md\nround46b-brief.md\nround46c-brief.md\nround46d-brief.md\nround46e-brief.md\nround46f-brief.md\nround46g-brief.md\nround46h-brief.md\nround46i-brief.md\nround46j-brief.md\nround46k-brief.md\nround46l-brief.md\nround46m-brief.md\nround46n-brief.md\nround46o-brief.md\nround46p-brief.md\nround46q-brief.md\nround46r-brief.md\nround46s-brief.md\nround46t-brief.md\nround46u-brief.md\nround46v-brief.md\nround46w-brief.md\nround46x-brief.md\nround46y-brief.md\nround46z-brief.md\nround47-brief.md\nround47b-brief.md\nround47c-brief.md\nround47d-brief.md\nround47e-brief.md\nround47f-brief.md\nround47g-brief.md\nround47h-brief.md\nround48-brief.md\nround49-brief.md\nround50-brief.md\nround51-brief.md\nround52-brief.md\nround53-brief.md\nround54-brief.md\nround55-brief.md\nround56-brief.md\nround56b-brief.md\nround56c-brief.md\nround57-brief.md\nround58-brief.md\nround59-brief.md\nround60-brief.md\nround61-brief.md\nround61b-brief.md\nround62-brief.md\nround63-brief.md\nround64-brief.md\nround65-brief.md\nround66-brief.md\nround67-brief.md\nround68-brief.md\nround69-brief.md\nround69b-brief.md\nround70-brief.md\ns4-ratestop-calc_small.py.txt\ns4-replay.log\ns4_census.py\ns4_replay.py\nsmall-cases.log\nsmall-mutants.log\nsmall-rehearsal.log\nsmall_cases.py\nsmall_mutants.py\nsmall_rehearsal.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba PAID-GATE.md && nl -ba blind_rules.py && wc -l paid_gate.py && rg -n '\"'^([A-Z]+[A-Z_0-9]* =|def |class )'\"' paid_gate.py\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13 paid gate: plan, harness and reading rule (registered before any send; D725, D729, D730)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result (D733): STOP.** All 72 answers were refused, and $0.3677 was spent; see `PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`.\n     4\t\n     5\t## 1. What is sent\n     6\t\n     7\t`paid_gate.py plan paid-plan.json` builds 12 requests from the stored runs.\n     8\t\n     9\t| Unit | Arm | Members | Evidence shown |\n    10\t|---|---|---|---|\n    11\t| pair-old-1 (09-20: v4 total, v8 Data Center) | joint; separate-v4; separate-v8 | both; one; one | the union of both stored requests' evidence in view (237 items), in every arm |\n    12\t| pair-old-2 (v14, v9) | joint; separate-v14; separate-v9 | as above | 237 |\n    13\t| pair-old-3 (v3, v35) | joint; separate-v3; separate-v35 | as above | 260 |\n    14\t| single-O (old-2 v29, equity commitments) | single | v29 | its own request's (35) |\n    15\t| single-S (old-2 v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 capex) | single | v6 | 31 |\n    16\t| single-E (old-3 v41, FY2028 Vera CPU) | single | v41 | 15 |\n    17\t\n    18\t- **Each request:** judging-v13's system text (`judging-v13-draft.txt`, 4,373 characters); the family header with the exact outcome\n    19\t  keys; the evidence; the themes once. No earlier forecast is shown (D728). The strict v13 schema.\n    20\t- **The model:** poc-v118's re-judging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium effort, 16,000 output tokens).\n    21\t- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\n    22\t- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\n    23\t  unit unresolved.\n    24\t- **What is scored:** the first attempt, on both arms (§3f). Retries are sent and recorded for diagnosis only.\n    25\t- **The separate arm:** its two first answers per pair and draw are merged and checked over the pair's family (C3, C4 across the two).\n    26\t\n    27\t## 2. Spend and stops\n    28\t\n    29\t- **The ledger:** one, at Alex's ceiling (`paid_gate.py send <folder> <ceiling> paid-plan.json` refuses any other ceiling).\n    30\t- **Budget:** the real budget transport and stop gate, which reserve each request's worst case before sending. After a stop, nothing\n    31\t  more is sent, and the remaining units are recorded as not sent.\n    32\t- **Estimate** (at `hivemind.model.PRICES`: gpt-6-luna, $0.10 input and $0.50 output per million tokens; tokens estimated as\n    33\t  characters / 4):\n    34\t  - a pair request is about 34–38k input tokens and a singleton 6–9k;\n    35\t  - the 36 first attempts cost about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n    36\t  - the transport reserves at most $0.039 for one request.\n    37\t  - **Proposed ceiling: $0.50.** It covers every scored attempt. Retries come last (§3g), so a ceiling stop among them leaves the\n    38\t    scored test complete.\n    39\t- **Sends:** one at a time, every first attempt before any retry (§3g). Each send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from\n    40\t  another.\n    41\t\n    42\t## 3. The $0 rehearsal (`paid_rehearsal.py`, `rehearsal.log`: 16 of 16)\n    43\t\n    44\t- **Clean run:** 36 first attempts, every HTTP body byte-equal to an independently built request, every unit published, the separate\n    45\t  arm reconciled in 9 of 9, the spend settled under the ceiling.\n    46\t- **Paths:**\n    47\t  - a refused calculation is retried, then published;\n    48\t  - two refusals give unresolved;\n    49\t  - a schema-invalid answer is retried;\n    50\t  - two separate answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3);\n    51\t  - after a ledger stop, nothing more is sent.\n    52\t- **Packets:** 27 packets with the arm hidden. The verdict is computed on synthetic readings: both arms good gives STOP (gain under 3);\n    53\t  a joint gain of 4 gives PASS; one published singleton defect gives STOP; a separate-arm defect alone does not stop; a missing\n    54\t  reading gives INCOMPLETE.\n    55\t\n    56\t## 3b. After council round 47 (`codex-r47.md`)\n    57\t\n    58\t- **[47.1] Reconciliation:** forecasts of the same quantity and scenario with equal recomputed values and bounds are unified before the\n    59\t  family's checks run. The duplicate's derivation is kept in results. Forecasts that differ stay as a conflict. Rehearsed: an agreeing\n    60\t  pair passes, and a disagreeing pair is refused (C4).\n    61\t- **[47.2] One authorization:**\n    62\t  - `paid-plan.sha256` pins the reviewed plan, and the sender refuses any other plan;\n    63\t  - `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json` is created exclusively at the first send, so a second launch is refused;\n    64\t  - (unit, arm) pairs are unique.\n    65\t- **[47.3] Every attempt recorded:**\n    66\t  - a `started` line is written before the provider is called;\n    67\t  - checker failures and arithmetic errors are refusals, recorded with the raw answer;\n    68\t  - every planned unit has a final status (`finals.json`), even after an abort;\n    69\t  - a refused reservation never reaches the provider.\n    70\t- **[47.4] Readings validated:** exact packets and cards, two readings (A, B) per card with yes or no and a ground for each question,\n    71\t  and a third reading on every disagreement. Otherwise the verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n    72\t- **[47.5] Packets:**\n    73\t  - the question text and ladder;\n    74\t  - each passage exactly as the request showed it, including those named only in `rests_on`;\n    75\t  - declared figures with renumbered ids, the recomputed outcomes and the recorded assumptions;\n    76\t  - the cards a non-reconciled separate unit has;\n    77\t  - neutral decision labels.\n    78\t- **Rehearsal:** 27 of 27 (`rehearsal.log`). The $0 gate still passes (`gate-run27.txt`: 87 of 87), and the mutants are unchanged.\n    79\t\n    80\t## 3c. After council round 47b (`codex-r47b.md`)\n    81\t\n    82\t- **[47b.1] Reconciliation:**\n    83\t  - Two recomputed values are the same when their bounds match and each end agrees within 1e-9 relative. A floating-point copy\n    84\t    unifies; a real difference stays a conflict.\n    85\t  - The readers never see the unified calculation. Each card of a reconciled packet is shown with its own original answer.\n    86\t- **[47b.2] Completeness comes from the attempt records.** `answers.jsonl` is the one record of what happened. For each planned unit\n    87\t  and draw, the final status is derived from it:\n    88\t  - no started line: **not sent**;\n    89\t  - a started line with no finished line: **interrupted**;\n    90\t  - a first refusal with no retry sent: **retry not sent**;\n    91\t  - otherwise, the last attempt's decision, and a second refusal is **unresolved**.\n    92\t\n    93\t  `results.json` is written from these records in a `finally`, so an abort still leaves it. The verdict is INCOMPLETE for every\n    94\t  status other than published, held or unresolved. That includes a reservation or HTTP failure, recorded as **transport**.\n    95\t- **[47b.3] Packets:**\n    96\t  - Every attempt of every card is listed, with neutral labels and check codes only.\n    97\t  - Each card is its own derivation: the figures its outcome and reference rest on, renumbered F1.. for that card alone.\n    98\t  - Its recorded assumptions are mapped to the same numbers. A record that names a figure outside the card is left out.\n    99\t- **[47b.4] Binding:**\n   100\t  - `packets.md` and the key are each created exclusively, once. A second `packets` call is refused.\n   101\t  - The key carries the run's digest (`answers.jsonl`, `results.json`, `plan.json`) and the sha256 of `packets.md`.\n   102\t  - The readings file carries the sha256 of the packets it was read on.\n   103\t  - The verdict is INCOMPLETE when any of the three differs, or when a ground is not a non-empty string naming a passage (e…) or a\n   104\t    figure (F…) of that packet.\n   105\t- **Rehearsal:** 41 of 41 (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   106\t  - a floating-point copy unifies;\n   107\t  - a reconciled card shows its own derivation;\n   108\t  - every attempt is listed;\n   109\t  - a transport failure makes the verdict INCOMPLETE;\n   110\t  - an interruption during a retry leaves results, marks the unit interrupted and the rest not sent;\n   111\t  - a retry that was never sent is incomplete;\n   112\t  - the card view maps assumption records and leaves out other cards';\n   113\t  - a second packets run, readings made on other packets, a run changed after freezing, and null or foreign grounds are each refused\n   114\t    or INCOMPLETE.\n   115\t- **Mutants:** 13 of 13 caught, and the control passes (`paid_mutants.py`, `paid-mutants.log`). Each mutant breaks one of these\n   116\t  defences on a scratch copy. The plan is unchanged (sha256 `6f81dae5…`), and `calc_check.py` is unchanged since gate run 27.\n   117\t\n   118\t## 3d. After council round 47c (`codex-r47c.md`)\n   119\t\n   120\t- **[47c.1] Reconciliation, by the joint arm's rule:**\n   121\t  - Only a forecast of a declared shared quantity is unified, and only with the other call's forecast of the same quantity and\n   122\t    scenario when their values are the same.\n   123\t  - Duplicates inside one call are never unified, so C3 and C4 judge them as they judge a joint answer.\n   124\t- **[47c.2] The key only orders the packets.**\n   125\t  - Each packet's decision, cards and allowed grounds come from the run.\n   126\t  - The verdict renders all packets again from the run and the key's order, and requires the text to equal `packets.md`, the key's\n   127\t    sha256 and the readings' sha256.\n   128\t  - The key must map exactly one packet to each unit of the run. A decision written into the key is ignored.\n   129\t- **[47c.3] Abstentions and attempts:**\n   130\t  - Each card is labelled K1, K2, … and is itself a valid ground, so a no-figure abstention can be read.\n   131\t  - Every earlier attempt shows its own answer, with figures named T<n>.F…. An attempt with no parsed answer shows its recorded\n   132\t    failure as a neutral label.\n   133\t  - Check codes are not shown: a cross-member code (C3, or C4 across members) occurs only in a joint answer and would reveal the arm.\n   134\t    The reasons stay in `results.json`.\n   135\t- **[47c.4] A torn journal:**\n   136\t  - A line that does not parse is skipped and listed as damaged. Its attempt counts as unfinished.\n   137\t  - `paid_gate.py recover <folder>` rebuilds `results.json` read-only and sends nothing.\n   138\t  - The verdict is INCOMPLETE while any line is damaged.\n   139\t- **Rehearsal:** 48 of 48, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   140\t  - two equal forecasts inside one answer, and two equal shared forecasts inside one call, are both refused after reconciliation, as\n   141\t    in a joint answer;\n   142\t  - an abstention reads with K1 as its ground;\n   143\t  - earlier attempts show their answers, with no codes;\n   144\t  - a key that maps packets to other units is INCOMPLETE;\n   145\t  - a decision written into the key changes nothing;\n   146\t  - a torn journal recovers with 35 units published and the torn one interrupted, and its verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n   147\t- **A rehearsal fault found and traced:** one parallel control run failed 47 of 48.\n   148\t  - The swap test exchanged P01 and P02. In about 2 of 26 shuffles, these are two draws of the same unit and arm.\n   149\t  - The rehearsal's draws answer alike, so their text is identical and the swap changes nothing.\n   150\t  - That is harmless to the verdict, which counts by unit, not by draw. The test now swaps two different units.\n   151\t- **Mutants:** 19 of 19 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   152\t  - Three missed in the first run and were traced:\n   153\t    - one was stale, because packets now render from the attempts;\n   154\t    - one was masked by the shared-only filter, and a shared within-call case was added;\n   155\t    - one disabled only half a condition.\n   156\t  - One mutant is equivalent and is left out: unifying any key across calls, not only declared shared ones. C3 looks only at\n   157\t    forecasts reachable from each member's own outcome, so the result does not change.\n   158\t\n   159\t## 3e. After council round 47d (`codex-r47d.md`): three structural rules\n   160\t\n   161\tRounds 47b to 47d kept finding the same two things: process information inside the readers' packets, and a mapping from packets to\n   162\tunits that could change after reading. These findings were answered by rule, not one by one.\n   163\t\n   164\t1. **The scoring text holds only what the four questions need.** For each card: the question, the ladder, the passages it names,\n   165\t   its own figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. It carries no attempt history, no code decision\n   166\t   and no check code. The verdict applies the code's decision itself.\n   167\t   - Earlier attempts go to `attempts.md`. That file is for diagnostic reading only and is never scored. Each attempt sits under its\n   168\t     own shuffled label (D01, …), with no link to a packet. [47d.3]\n   169\t   - A card with no final answer says why in plain words: no request was sent; the request was started and no answer was recorded;\n   170\t     no answer arrived; the answer was refused and its retry was not sent; or the answer did not match the format. [47d.4]\n   171\t2. **The text the readers receive commits to the mapping.** The key is {a random salt, the run's digest, the packet order, the\n   172\t   attempt labels}. Its sha256 is the first line of `packets.md`. The verdict refuses a key whose sha256 differs from that line. It\n   173\t   also renders the packets again from the run and the key, and refuses a mismatch with `packets.md` or with the readings' sha256.\n   174\t   A swap of two packets with identical text is caught, and so is a decision written into the key. [47d.1]\n   175\t3. **Reconciliation is one to one.** A declared shared forecast is unified only when each of the two calls holds exactly one\n   176\t   candidate for that quantity and scenario, and their values are the same. Otherwise every copy stays, for C3 and C4 to judge as in a\n   177\t   joint answer. [47d.2]\n   178\t\n   179\t- **The record:** an attempt that was started and not finished is kept in `results.json` as interrupted.\n   180\t- **Rehearsal:** 51 of 51, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   181\t  - the scoring text has no attempt, decision or code;\n   182\t  - the refused first answer appears only in `attempts.md`;\n   183\t  - a swap of identical-text packets is INCOMPLETE;\n   184\t  - a forged key is INCOMPLETE;\n   185\t  - two equal shared forecasts in the second call are refused (C4, three nodes);\n   186\t  - an interrupted card says the request was started.\n   187\t- **Mutants:** 20 of 20 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   188\t\n   189\t## 3f. After council round 47e (`codex-r47e.md`)\n   190\t\n   191\t- **[47e.1] The first attempt is scored, on both arms.**\n   192\t  - In the joint arm, a cross-card conflict (C3) is refused and retried with its reason, so the retry can repair it. In the separate\n   193\t    arm, the same conflict appears only when the two answers are reconciled, after both calls are over, and there is no retry.\n   194\t  - Scoring the final answers would credit the joint arm with a second chance the separate arm cannot have.\n   195\t  - D725 registered both arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about retries. Its pass and stop lines stay as\n   196\t    written and are applied to the first attempts.\n   197\t  - Retries are still sent and read for diagnosis (`attempts.md`), and are not counted.\n   198\t  - Rehearsed: the joint pair is published after its retry, but its refused first attempt is scored, so both arms come out at 6.\n   199\t- **[47e.2] One unit.** A shared forecast is unified only when the two copies have the same unit, as well as the same value and bounds.\n   200\t  Rehearsed: 110 USD bn against 110 USD is refused (C4).\n   201\t- **[47e.3] Every returned text is readable.**\n   202\t  - When the format check fails an answer, the scoring packet keeps its neutral label.\n   203\t  - The text the model returned, and the passages it names, go to `attempts.md` under a blind label. This covers both a first attempt\n   204\t    and a final one that fails the format.\n   205\t- **[47e.4] One verdict per run.**\n   206\t  - `verdict` copies the readings into the run once (`readings.json`, created exclusively).\n   207\t  - It scores them and writes `verdict.json` once, holding the readings' sha256, the key commitment, the packets' sha256, the run digest\n   208\t    and the result.\n   209\t  - A second verdict on the run is refused. `paid_gate.py replay` recomputes from the sealed readings and must reproduce the result.\n   210\t  - Rehearsed: the second verdict is refused; replay reproduces the result; after the sealed readings are edited, replay fails.\n   211\t- **Rehearsal:** 55 of 55, run three times (`rehearsal.log`).\n   212\t- **Mutants:** 25 of 25 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   213\t  - Two obsolete mutants were repointed or removed.\n   214\t  - One mutant crashed on a missing file and not on the defence. The test was corrected, and the mutant now fails the right check.\n   215\t\n   216\t## 3g. After council round 47f (`codex-r47f.md`)\n   217\t\n   218\t- **[47f.1] Retries cannot decide whether the scored test is complete.**\n   219\t  - The run sends every first attempt (all 36) before any retry.\n   220\t  - Completeness is judged on the first attempts: each must end published, held or refused.\n   221\t  - A retry that fails in transport, is interrupted or is never sent stays in the diagnostic record.\n   222\t  - Rehearsed: an interruption during a retry leaves all 36 scored attempts and a complete verdict. A transport failure on a retry\n   223\t    leaves the verdict complete. An interruption during a scored attempt makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. In the journal, every first\n   224\t    attempt comes before every retry.\n   225\t- **[47f.2] Every returned text survives.**\n   226\t  - The record keeps the provider's whole response, as the archive stores it, with no 20,000-character cut.\n   227\t  - A null content is shown as the model's refusal, or as \"no text returned\".\n   228\t  - Both files are rendered before anything is written, and a failed render leaves no files.\n   229\t  - Rehearsed: a refusal with null content, a 25,000-character malformed answer whose passage is named at its end, and a render that\n   230\t    fails and then succeeds.\n   231\t- **Rehearsal:** 61 of 61, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   232\t- **Mutants:** 30 of 30 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`). Two mutants are caught by the crash the defence prevents:\n   233\t  - without the interrupted branch, the summary fails on an unfinished attempt;\n   234\t  - passing a null content on, packet rendering fails.\n   235\t\n   236\t## 3h. After council round 47g (`codex-r47g.md`)\n   237\t\n   238\t- **[47g] Two journals, read on the writer's own delimiter.**\n   239\t  - Scored first attempts are written to `answers.jsonl`, and diagnostic retries to `retries.jsonl`. The run digest covers both.\n   240\t  - A damaged line in `answers.jsonl` makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. A damaged line in `retries.jsonl` is reported and marks that retry\n   241\t    interrupted, but leaves the scored test complete.\n   242\t  - Records are split on '\\n' only, the writer's delimiter. An answer may contain other Unicode line separators (U+2028, U+0085,\n   243\t    U+2029), and these are kept inside the record.\n   244\t  - Rehearsed: a torn retry record leaves the verdict complete; a torn scored record (the existing control) makes it INCOMPLETE; an\n   245\t    answer holding U+2028, U+0085 and U+2029 stays one record; the order of every first attempt before any retry is checked on the\n   246\t    provider's own call sequence.\n   247\t- **Rehearsal:** 63 of 63, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   248\t- **Mutants:** 33 of 33 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   249\t  - One mutant (splitting on any line break) is caught when a scenario guard stops the rehearsal: 36 attempts started, 35 finished.\n   250\t  - The mutant harness now counts such a stop as a catch and shows its reason.\n   251\t\n   252\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   276\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   277\t\n   278\t## 5. What the result decides\n   279\t\n   280\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   281\t  step Alex opens.\n   282\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n     1\t\"\"\"The one source of the defect definitions and the writer's format material for judging-v13s blind readers and adjudicators (D744).\n     2\t\n     3\tReaders and adjudicators get the same text: the writer's system text, every schema description, and these definitions, so that what\n     4\tthe format rules permit is never marked as a defect by one and cleared by the other.\n     5\t\"\"\"\n     6\timport json\n     7\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     8\t\n     9\tDEFINITIONS = \"\"\"Definitions (judge each against the passages and the format rules the writer was given, shown below; what the format rules permit is\n    10\tnot a defect):\n    11\t- supported: the forecast follows from the shown passages and the answer's stated assumptions; a reader could check it against them.\n    12\t  For a forecast, the assumption that decides the band must rest on the passages in one of three ways: its size, a bound that\n    13\t  justifies the rung, or, when the passages do not give the asked quantity, a related figure that the answer explains. An explained\n    14\t  related figure satisfies this requirement even though the other side of the line remains possible. It is explained when the\n    15\t  answer says why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked, and why, under the answer's own stated\n    16\t  assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely; an answer that does not explain this is not supported (a ruling). For an unresolved\n    17\t  member, supported means its reason holds: after the strongest relevant passages, a gap remains that keeps the rung unsettled (a\n    18\t  ruling).\n    19\t- number misread: a source figure's number, scale, sign or qualifier differs from what its passage's quote writes, allowing what the\n    20\t  format rules permit.\n    21\t- wrong arithmetic: a computed figure does not equal its operation on its inputs, within the tolerance the format rules state.\n    22\t- part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n    23\t  includes it (directly or through an intermediate figure or an estimate).\n    24\t- two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n    25\t  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n    26\t  calculation (a ruling). Look through any rate or multiple, including inside a stated assumption, for a second dollar value of the\n    27\t  quarter.\n    28\t- own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n    29\t  estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n    30\t  applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n    31\t- broken structure: a link that does not resolve, a figure that depends on itself, a missing or doubled answer, an outcome that is not\n    32\t  the question's quantity, or a rung whose band does not hold the outcome. For a range outcome, the format allows \"a band it overlaps,\n    33\t  with the reason in reasons\": such a rung is not broken structure; a band the range does not reach is. A total used for a narrower\n    34\t  quantity (total capital expenditure for data-center spending) without a stated deduction or a supported bound is an outcome not of\n    35\t  the question's quantity (a ruling).\"\"\"\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef descriptions(schema, path=''):\n    39\t    \"\"\"Every description in the schema, keyed by its field path.\"\"\"\n    40\t    found = {}\n    41\t    if isinstance(schema, dict):\n    42\t        if isinstance(schema.get('description'), str):\n    43\t            found[path.strip('/') or 'answer'] = schema['description']\n    44\t        for key, value in schema.items():\n    45\t            if key != 'description':\n    46\t                step = '' if key in ('properties', 'items', 'anyOf') else key\n    47\t                found.update(descriptions(value, f'{path}/{step}' if step else path))\n    48\t    elif isinstance(schema, list):\n    49\t        for value in schema:\n    50\t            found.update(descriptions(value, path))\n    51\t    return found\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef allowed_qualifiers(schema):\n    55\t    \"\"\"The qualifier values the writer's own schema allowed (D747: an older run's schema, not today's list).\"\"\"\n    56\t    options = schema['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']['qualifier']['anyOf']\n    57\t    found = [o['enum'] for o in options if isinstance(o, dict) and 'enum' in o]\n    58\t    if len(found) != 1:\n    59\t        raise SystemExit('the schema does not hold exactly one qualifier list')\n    60\t    return found[0]\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef format_material(case_folder):\n    64\t    \"\"\"The writer's system text and every schema description, as shown to readers and adjudicators.\"\"\"\n    65\t    case_folder = Path(case_folder)\n    66\t    schema = json.loads((case_folder / 'schema.json').read_text())\n    67\t    return '\\n'.join(['# The system text the writer was given', (case_folder / 'system.txt').read_text(), '',\n    68\t                      '# The format rules the writer was given (schema descriptions)',\n    69\t                      json.dumps(descriptions(schema), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False), '',\n    70\t                      'The qualifier values the format allows (a qualifier not in this list cannot be recorded): '\n    71\t                      + ', '.join(allowed_qualifiers(schema)) + '.'])\n     818 paid_gate.py\n23:HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n24:REPO = HERE.parents[2]\n32:RUN = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n33:CONFIG = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'                              # its re-judging model setting: gpt-6-luna, medium, 16000 output tokens\n34:SYSTEM = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\n35:SYSTEM_S = (HERE / 'judging-v13s.txt').read_text()                      # the small format (D737): one sentence changed\n36:CHECKERS = {None: cc, 'v13': cc, 'v13s': cs}\n37:APPROVED_CEILING = 0.5                                                  # Alex, 2026-11-22 (D732): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\"\n38:PINNED_PLAN_SHA256 = (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').read_text().strip() if (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').exists() else None\n39:AUTH = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json'\n41:PINNED_PLAN_V13S = (HERE / 'paid-plan-v13s.sha256').read_text().strip() if (HERE / 'paid-plan-v13s.sha256').exists() else None\n42:AUTH_V13S = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/authorization.json'\n43:DRAWS = (1, 2, 3)\n44:RETRY_MARK = '\\n\\nThe code refused the previous answer because: '\n45:PAIRS = [('old-1', ('v4', 9014), ('v8', 9022)), ('old-2', ('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)), ('old-3', ('v3', 9183), ('v35', 9177))]\n46:SINGLETONS = [('O', 'old-2', 'v29', 8734, ('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', 'company', 'end of FY2027')),\n51:def W(population, measure, scope, period):\n55:def bands(draw, view_id):\n61:def passages(draw, evidence_ids):\n69:def pair_family(draw, total, dc):\n77:def only(family, view_id):\n84:def small_family(family, part_scopes=(), notes=None):\n96:PAIR_SCOPES = [{'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'part': 'Data Center', 'whole': 'company'}]\n97:O_NOTE = 'the balance at the end of FY2027, as the FY2027 annual report publishes it'\n100:def checker(fmt):\n104:def decode(data, fmt, family):\n109:def questions(draw, view_ids):\n119:def shown_lines(user):\n129:def item(unit, arm, draw, calls, family, shown, fmt='v13'):\n142:def build_plan(fmt='v13'):\n161:def plan(out, fmt='v13'):\n180:def strip(data):\n184:class Gate:\n252:JOURNALS = ('answers.jsonl', 'retries.jsonl')\n255:def attempt_records(out, damaged=None):\n274:ATTEMPT_FIELDS = ('attempt', 'status', 'decision', 'errors', 'data', 'raw')\n277:def first_attempt(entry):\n283:def derive_finals(out, items, damaged=None):\n311:def summarise(out, items, ledger_state):\n336:def _same_value(a, b):\n343:def merge(parts, shared_keys, ck=cc):\n414:def recover(out):\n423:def budget_module():\n431:def send(out, approved, plan_path):\n473:QUESTIONS = {'usable': 'the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on',\n479:def normalise(calc, prefix=''):\n505:def run_digest(out):\n513:def card_view(calc, view_id, recorded, prefix='', ck=cc):\n535:NO_ANSWER = {'not sent': 'No request was sent for this card.', 'interrupted': 'The request was started; no answer was recorded.',\n537:FORMAT_INVALID = 'The answer did not match the required format.'\n540:def packet_units(results, items):\n557:def card_lines(base, fam, v, token, data, final_label, prefix=''):\n580:def packet_body(items, unit, arm, decision, per_card):\n601:def key_commitment(key):\n605:def render_packets(out, key):\n621:def returned_text(raw):\n638:def render_attempts(out, labels):\n662:def packets(out, key_dir):\n691:def _grounded(ground, grounds):\n696:def final_readings(pid, cards, members, grounds=()):\n719:def verdict(out, readings_path, key_dir):\n737:def replay(out, key_dir):\n749:def score(out, key_dir):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
