{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && { rg -n '\"'^#|first attempt|§4|packets|incomplete|INCOMPLETE|refus|8 of'\"' PAID-GATE.md; nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | head -58; }\"","aggregated_output":"1:# judging-v13 paid gate: plan, harness and reading rule (registered before any send; D725, D729, D730)\n3:**Result (D733): STOP.** All 72 answers were refused, and $0.3677 was spent; see `PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`.\n5:## 1. What is sent\n21:- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\n22:- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\n24:- **What is scored:** the first attempt, on both arms (§3f). Retries are sent and recorded for diagnosis only.\n27:## 2. Spend and stops\n29:- **The ledger:** one, at Alex's ceiling (`paid_gate.py send <folder> <ceiling> paid-plan.json` refuses any other ceiling).\n35:  - the 36 first attempts cost about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n39:- **Sends:** one at a time, every first attempt before any retry (§3g). Each send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from\n42:## 3. The $0 rehearsal (`paid_rehearsal.py`, `rehearsal.log`: 16 of 16)\n44:- **Clean run:** 36 first attempts, every HTTP body byte-equal to an independently built request, every unit published, the separate\n47:  - a refused calculation is retried, then published;\n48:  - two refusals give unresolved;\n50:  - two separate answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3);\n52:- **Packets:** 27 packets with the arm hidden. The verdict is computed on synthetic readings: both arms good gives STOP (gain under 3);\n54:  reading gives INCOMPLETE.\n56:## 3b. After council round 47 (`codex-r47.md`)\n60:  pair passes, and a disagreeing pair is refused (C4).\n62:  - `paid-plan.sha256` pins the reviewed plan, and the sender refuses any other plan;\n63:  - `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json` is created exclusively at the first send, so a second launch is refused;\n67:  - checker failures and arithmetic errors are refusals, recorded with the raw answer;\n69:  - a refused reservation never reaches the provider.\n70:- **[47.4] Readings validated:** exact packets and cards, two readings (A, B) per card with yes or no and a ground for each question,\n71:  and a third reading on every disagreement. Otherwise the verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n80:## 3c. After council round 47b (`codex-r47b.md`)\n90:  - a first refusal with no retry sent: **retry not sent**;\n91:  - otherwise, the last attempt's decision, and a second refusal is **unresolved**.\n93:  `results.json` is written from these records in a `finally`, so an abort still leaves it. The verdict is INCOMPLETE for every\n100:  - `packets.md` and the key are each created exclusively, once. A second `packets` call is refused.\n101:  - The key carries the run's digest (`answers.jsonl`, `results.json`, `plan.json`) and the sha256 of `packets.md`.\n102:  - The readings file carries the sha256 of the packets it was read on.\n103:  - The verdict is INCOMPLETE when any of the three differs, or when a ground is not a non-empty string naming a passage (e…) or a\n109:  - a transport failure makes the verdict INCOMPLETE;\n111:  - a retry that was never sent is incomplete;\n113:  - a second packets run, readings made on other packets, a run changed after freezing, and null or foreign grounds are each refused\n114:    or INCOMPLETE.\n118:## 3d. After council round 47c (`codex-r47c.md`)\n124:- **[47c.2] The key only orders the packets.**\n126:  - The verdict renders all packets again from the run and the key's order, and requires the text to equal `packets.md`, the key's\n138:  - The verdict is INCOMPLETE while any line is damaged.\n139:- **Rehearsal:** 48 of 48, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n140:  - two equal forecasts inside one answer, and two equal shared forecasts inside one call, are both refused after reconciliation, as\n144:  - a key that maps packets to other units is INCOMPLETE;\n146:  - a torn journal recovers with 35 units published and the torn one interrupted, and its verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n153:    - one was stale, because packets now render from the attempts;\n159:## 3e. After council round 47d (`codex-r47d.md`): three structural rules\n161:Rounds 47b to 47d kept finding the same two things: process information inside the readers' packets, and a mapping from packets to\n170:     no answer arrived; the answer was refused and its retry was not sent; or the answer did not match the format. [47d.4]\n172:   attempt labels}. Its sha256 is the first line of `packets.md`. The verdict refuses a key whose sha256 differs from that line. It\n173:   also renders the packets again from the run and the key, and refuses a mismatch with `packets.md` or with the readings' sha256.\n174:   A swap of two packets with identical text is caught, and so is a decision written into the key. [47d.1]\n182:  - the refused first answer appears only in `attempts.md`;\n183:  - a swap of identical-text packets is INCOMPLETE;\n184:  - a forged key is INCOMPLETE;\n185:  - two equal shared forecasts in the second call are refused (C4, three nodes);\n189:## 3f. After council round 47e (`codex-r47e.md`)\n191:- **[47e.1] The first attempt is scored, on both arms.**\n192:  - In the joint arm, a cross-card conflict (C3) is refused and retried with its reason, so the retry can repair it. In the separate\n196:    written and are applied to the first attempts.\n198:  - Rehearsed: the joint pair is published after its retry, but its refused first attempt is scored, so both arms come out at 6.\n200:  Rehearsed: 110 USD bn against 110 USD is refused (C4).\n203:  - The text the model returned, and the passages it names, go to `attempts.md` under a blind label. This covers both a first attempt\n207:  - It scores them and writes `verdict.json` once, holding the readings' sha256, the key commitment, the packets' sha256, the run digest\n209:  - A second verdict on the run is refused. `paid_gate.py replay` recomputes from the sealed readings and must reproduce the result.\n210:  - Rehearsed: the second verdict is refused; replay reproduces the result; after the sealed readings are edited, replay fails.\n216:## 3g. After council round 47f (`codex-r47f.md`)\n219:  - The run sends every first attempt (all 36) before any retry.\n220:  - Completeness is judged on the first attempts: each must end published, held or refused.\n223:    leaves the verdict complete. An interruption during a scored attempt makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. In the journal, every first\n227:  - A null content is shown as the model's refusal, or as \"no text returned\".\n229:  - Rehearsed: a refusal with null content, a 25,000-character malformed answer whose passage is named at its end, and a render that\n236:## 3h. After council round 47g (`codex-r47g.md`)\n239:  - Scored first attempts are written to `answers.jsonl`, and diagnostic retries to `retries.jsonl`. The run digest covers both.\n240:  - A damaged line in `answers.jsonl` makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. A damaged line in `retries.jsonl` is reported and marks that retry\n244:  - Rehearsed: a torn retry record leaves the verdict complete; a torn scored record (the existing control) makes it INCOMPLETE; an\n245:    answer holding U+2028, U+0085 and U+2029 stays one record; the order of every first attempt before any retry is checked on the\n252:## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n254:- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n261:  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n270:- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n271:  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n275:  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n278:## 5. What the result decides\n282:- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n     1\t# judging-v13 paid gate: plan, harness and reading rule (registered before any send; D725, D729, D730)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result (D733): STOP.** All 72 answers were refused, and $0.3677 was spent; see `PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`.\n     4\t\n     5\t## 1. What is sent\n     6\t\n     7\t`paid_gate.py plan paid-plan.json` builds 12 requests from the stored runs.\n     8\t\n     9\t| Unit | Arm | Members | Evidence shown |\n    10\t|---|---|---|---|\n    11\t| pair-old-1 (09-20: v4 total, v8 Data Center) | joint; separate-v4; separate-v8 | both; one; one | the union of both stored requests' evidence in view (237 items), in every arm |\n    12\t| pair-old-2 (v14, v9) | joint; separate-v14; separate-v9 | as above | 237 |\n    13\t| pair-old-3 (v3, v35) | joint; separate-v3; separate-v35 | as above | 260 |\n    14\t| single-O (old-2 v29, equity commitments) | single | v29 | its own request's (35) |\n    15\t| single-S (old-2 v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 capex) | single | v6 | 31 |\n    16\t| single-E (old-3 v41, FY2028 Vera CPU) | single | v41 | 15 |\n    17\t\n    18\t- **Each request:** judging-v13's system text (`judging-v13-draft.txt`, 4,373 characters); the family header with the exact outcome\n    19\t  keys; the evidence; the themes once. No earlier forecast is shown (D728). The strict v13 schema.\n    20\t- **The model:** poc-v118's re-judging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium effort, 16,000 output tokens).\n    21\t- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\n    22\t- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\n    23\t  unit unresolved.\n    24\t- **What is scored:** the first attempt, on both arms (§3f). Retries are sent and recorded for diagnosis only.\n    25\t- **The separate arm:** its two first answers per pair and draw are merged and checked over the pair's family (C3, C4 across the two).\n    26\t\n    27\t## 2. Spend and stops\n    28\t\n    29\t- **The ledger:** one, at Alex's ceiling (`paid_gate.py send <folder> <ceiling> paid-plan.json` refuses any other ceiling).\n    30\t- **Budget:** the real budget transport and stop gate, which reserve each request's worst case before sending. After a stop, nothing\n    31\t  more is sent, and the remaining units are recorded as not sent.\n    32\t- **Estimate** (at `hivemind.model.PRICES`: gpt-6-luna, $0.10 input and $0.50 output per million tokens; tokens estimated as\n    33\t  characters / 4):\n    34\t  - a pair request is about 34–38k input tokens and a singleton 6–9k;\n    35\t  - the 36 first attempts cost about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n    36\t  - the transport reserves at most $0.039 for one request.\n    37\t  - **Proposed ceiling: $0.50.** It covers every scored attempt. Retries come last (§3g), so a ceiling stop among them leaves the\n    38\t    scored test complete.\n    39\t- **Sends:** one at a time, every first attempt before any retry (§3g). Each send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from\n    40\t  another.\n    41\t\n    42\t## 3. The $0 rehearsal (`paid_rehearsal.py`, `rehearsal.log`: 16 of 16)\n    43\t\n    44\t- **Clean run:** 36 first attempts, every HTTP body byte-equal to an independently built request, every unit published, the separate\n    45\t  arm reconciled in 9 of 9, the spend settled under the ceiling.\n    46\t- **Paths:**\n    47\t  - a refused calculation is retried, then published;\n    48\t  - two refusals give unresolved;\n    49\t  - a schema-invalid answer is retried;\n    50\t  - two separate answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3);\n    51\t  - after a ledger stop, nothing more is sent.\n    52\t- **Packets:** 27 packets with the arm hidden. The verdict is computed on synthetic readings: both arms good gives STOP (gain under 3);\n    53\t  a joint gain of 4 gives PASS; one published singleton defect gives STOP; a separate-arm defect alone does not stop; a missing\n    54\t  reading gives INCOMPLETE.\n    55\t\n    56\t## 3b. After council round 47 (`codex-r47.md`)\n    57\t\n    58\t- **[47.1] Reconciliation:** forecasts of the same quantity and scenario with equal recomputed values and bounds are unified before the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && { nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '283,335p;414,480p;479,621p'; }\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && { nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '283,335p;414,480p;479,621p'; }\"","aggregated_output":"   283\tdef derive_finals(out, items, damaged=None):\n   284\t    \"\"\"Each planned unit and draw: 'dispatched' (a started line), 'completed' (a finished line), and the decision of its last finished\n   285\t    attempt (a second refusal is unresolved). A unit with no started line is not sent; one started but not finished is interrupted.\"\"\"\n   286\t    records = attempt_records(out, damaged)\n   287\t    finals = {}\n   288\t    for it in items:\n   289\t        for draw in DRAWS:\n   290\t            mine = [r for r in records if r['unit'] == it['unit'] and r['arm'] == it['arm'] and r['draw'] == draw]\n   291\t            started = [r for r in mine if r['status'] == 'started']\n   292\t            done = [r for r in mine if r['status'] != 'started']\n   293\t            key = f'{it[\"unit\"]}|{it[\"arm\"]}|{draw}'\n   294\t            if not started:\n   295\t                finals[key] = {'decision': 'not sent', 'attempts': []}\n   296\t                continue\n   297\t            if len(done) < len(started):\n   298\t                unfinished = [{'attempt': r['attempt'], 'status': 'interrupted', 'decision': 'interrupted'} for r in started\n   299\t                              if r['attempt'] not in {d['attempt'] for d in done}]\n   300\t                finals[key] = {'decision': 'interrupted', 'attempts': [{k: r.get(k) for k in ATTEMPT_FIELDS} for r in done] + unfinished}\n   301\t                continue\n   302\t            last = done[-1]\n   303\t            decision = last['decision']\n   304\t            if decision == 'refused':                          # a second refusal is unresolved; a first with no retry sent is incomplete\n   305\t                decision = 'unresolved' if len(done) >= 2 else 'retry not sent'\n   306\t            finals[key] = {k: last.get(k) for k in ('status', 'data', 'errors', 'recorded', 'published')}\n   307\t            finals[key].update(decision=decision, attempts=[{k: r.get(k) for k in ATTEMPT_FIELDS} for r in done])\n   308\t    return finals\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\tdef summarise(out, items, ledger_state):\n   312\t    damaged = []\n   313\t    finals = derive_finals(out, items, damaged)\n   314\t    reconciled = {}\n   315\t    fmt = items[0].get('format') if items else None\n   316\t    ck = checker(fmt)\n   317\t    for draw_store, total, dc in PAIRS:                     # the separate arm, reconciled over the pair's family\n   318\t        for draw in DRAWS:\n   319\t            a, b = (first_attempt(finals.get(f'pair-{draw_store}|separate-{m[0]}|{draw}', {})) for m in (total, dc))   # [47e.1]\n   320\t            if a.get('decision') != 'publish' or b.get('decision') != 'publish':\n   321\t                reconciled[f'pair-{draw_store}|{draw}'] = {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': [a.get('decision'), b.get('decision')]}\n   322\t                continue\n   323\t            joint = next(i for i in items if i['unit'] == f'pair-{draw_store}' and i['arm'] == 'joint')\n   324\t            family = joint['family'] if fmt == 'v13s' else pair_family(draw_store, total, dc)\n   325\t            merged = merge([(total[0], decode(a['data'], fmt, family)), (dc[0], decode(b['data'], fmt, family))],\n   326\t                           {ck._key(s) for s in family['shared']}, ck)\n   327\t            pas = joint['passages']\n   328\t            result = ck.check(family, pas, {k: merged[k] for k in ('figures', 'answers')})\n   329\t            reconciled[f'pair-{draw_store}|{draw}'] = {'decision': ck.publish_decision(family, merged, result), 'errors': result['errors'],\n   330\t                                                     'published': result.get('published'), 'calc': merged}\n   331\t    summary = {'finals': finals, 'reconciled': reconciled, 'ledger': ledger_state, 'damaged': damaged}\n   332\t    (out / 'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   333\t    return summary\n   334\t\n   335\t\n   414\tdef recover(out):\n   415\t    \"\"\"Read-only: rebuild results.json from the journal of a stopped run; nothing is sent.\"\"\"\n   416\t    items = json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())\n   417\t    ledger = json.loads((out / 'ledger.json').read_text()) if (out / 'ledger.json').exists() else None\n   418\t    summary = summarise(out, items, ledger)\n   419\t    print(json.dumps({'damaged': summary['damaged'], 'finals': {k: v['decision'] for k, v in summary['finals'].items()}}, indent=1))\n   420\t    return summary\n   421\t\n   422\t\n   423\tdef budget_module():\n   424\t    import importlib.util\n   425\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('budget_replay_v13', REPO / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n   426\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   427\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n   428\t    return module\n   429\t\n   430\t\n   431\tdef send(out, approved, plan_path):\n   432\t    if APPROVED_CEILING is None or approved != APPROVED_CEILING:\n   433\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling is {APPROVED_CEILING} (Alex names it); refused')\n   434\t    if out.exists():\n   435\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} exists: the gate starts from an empty folder')\n   436\t    text = Path(plan_path).read_text()\n   437\t    items = json.loads(text)\n   438\t    formats = {i.get('format') for i in items}\n   439\t    if formats == {'v13s'}:                                                  # D753: the v13s re-send has its own pin and authorization\n   440\t        pin, auth = PINNED_PLAN_V13S, AUTH_V13S\n   441\t    elif 'v13s' in formats:\n   442\t        raise SystemExit('the plan mixes formats; refused')\n   443\t    else:\n   444\t        pin, auth = PINNED_PLAN_SHA256, AUTH\n   445\t    if pin is None or hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest() != pin:          # [47.2] only the reviewed plan\n   446\t        raise SystemExit('the plan is not the reviewed one (sha256 differs); refused')\n   447\t    auth.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   448\t    try:                                                                     # [47.2] one authorization, one ledger, one launch\n   449\t        with open(auth, 'x') as handle:\n   450\t            json.dump({'plan_sha256': pin, 'ceiling': approved, 'out': str(out)}, handle)\n   451\t    except FileExistsError:\n   452\t        raise SystemExit(f'{auth} exists: this authorization was already used; refused')\n   453\t    if len({(i['unit'], i['arm']) for i in items}) != len(items):\n   454\t        raise SystemExit('duplicate (unit, arm) in the plan; refused')\n   455\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n   456\t    (out / 'plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(items))\n   457\t    budget = budget_module()\n   458\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(out / 'ledger.json'), approved)\n   459\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(out / 'ledger.json'))\n   460\t    lock_handle = open(out / 'gate.launcher.lock', 'a+')\n   461\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher('v13-gate', lock_handle):\n   462\t        raise SystemExit('another launch is running')\n   463\t    remove_gate = budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   464\t    try:\n   465\t        summary = Gate(out, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger).run(items)\n   466\t    finally:\n   467\t        remove_gate()\n   468\t        ledger.remove_launcher('v13-gate')\n   469\t    print(json.dumps({k: v.get('decision') for k, v in summary['finals'].items()}, indent=1))\n   470\t\n   471\t\n   472\t# ---------- blind reading ----------\n   473\tQUESTIONS = {'usable': 'the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on',\n   474\t             'contradiction': 'with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction',\n   475\t             'internal_reference': \"the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation\",\n   476\t             'deciding_gap': 'an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band'}\n   477\t\n   478\t\n   479\tdef normalise(calc, prefix=''):\n   479\tdef normalise(calc, prefix=''):\n   480\t    \"\"\"Figure ids renumbered F1.. (after `prefix`) and member prefixes removed, so the arm cannot be read from the ids.\"\"\"\n   480\t    \"\"\"Figure ids renumbered F1.. (after `prefix`) and member prefixes removed, so the arm cannot be read from the ids.\"\"\"\n   481\t    rename = {f['id']: f'{prefix}F{n}' for n, f in enumerate(calc['figures'], 1)}\n   482\t    out = []\n   483\t    for f in calc['figures']:\n   484\t        g = dict(f, id=rename[f['id']])\n   485\t        for key in ('inputs', 'rests_on', 'converts'):\n   486\t            if key in g:\n   487\t                g[key] = [rename.get(x, x) for x in g[key]]\n   488\t        for key in ('disputed', 'bridge'):\n   489\t            if key in g:\n   490\t                g[key] = rename.get(g[key], g[key])\n   491\t        if 'adjusts' in g:\n   492\t            g['adjusts'] = dict(g['adjusts'], figure=rename.get(g['adjusts']['figure'], g['adjusts']['figure']))\n   493\t        out.append(g)\n   494\t    answers = []\n   495\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   496\t        a2 = dict(a)\n   497\t        if 'outcome' in a2:\n   498\t            a2['outcome'] = rename.get(a2['outcome'], a2['outcome'])\n   499\t        if (a2.get('reference') or {}).get('figure'):\n   500\t            a2['reference'] = {'figure': rename.get(a2['reference']['figure'], a2['reference']['figure'])}\n   501\t        answers.append(a2)\n   502\t    return {'figures': out, 'answers': answers}, rename\n   503\t\n   504\t\n   505\tdef run_digest(out):\n   506\t    h = hashlib.sha256()\n   507\t    for name in ('answers.jsonl', 'retries.jsonl', 'results.json', 'plan.json'):\n   508\t        path = out / name\n   509\t        h.update(name.encode() + b'\\0' + (path.read_bytes() if path.exists() else b''))\n   510\t    return h.hexdigest()\n   511\t\n   512\t\n   513\tdef card_view(calc, view_id, recorded, prefix='', ck=cc):\n   514\t    \"\"\"[47b.3] One card as its own derivation: the figures its outcome and reference rest on, renumbered F1.. (after `prefix`) for this\n   515\t    card alone, and the recorded assumptions about its outcome or its own figures mapped to the same numbers.\"\"\"\n   516\t    figs = {f['id']: f for f in calc['figures']}\n   517\t    refs = lambda f: list(f.get('inputs', [])) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs] + \\\n   518\t        ([f['adjusts']['figure']] if f.get('adjusts') else []) + ([f['bridge']] if f.get('bridge') else [])\n   519\t    ans = next(a for a in calc['answers'] if a['view_id'] == view_id)\n   520\t    own = set()\n   521\t    for start in (ans.get('outcome'), (ans.get('reference') or {}).get('figure')):\n   522\t        if start in figs:\n   523\t            own |= ck._upstream_of(start, figs, refs) | {start}\n   524\t    sub = {'figures': [f for f in calc['figures'] if f['id'] in own], 'answers': [ans]}\n   525\t    norm, rename = normalise(sub, prefix)\n   526\t    mapped = []\n   527\t    for r in recorded:                                    # an assumption about this card's outcome, or about one of its own figures\n   528\t        named = [r[k] for k in ('figure', 'bridge') if isinstance(r.get(k), str)]\n   529\t        if (r.get('outcome') == view_id or any(n in rename for n in named)) and all(n in rename for n in named):\n   530\t            mapped.append({k: rename[v] if k in ('figure', 'bridge') else v for k, v in r.items()})\n   531\t    return norm, mapped, sorted({f['evidence'] for f in sub['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} | set(ans.get('cites', []))\n   532\t                                | {x for f in sub['figures'] for x in f.get('rests_on', []) if str(x).startswith('e')})\n   533\t\n   534\t\n   535\tNO_ANSWER = {'not sent': 'No request was sent for this card.', 'interrupted': 'The request was started; no answer was recorded.',\n   536\t             'transport': 'No answer arrived.', 'retry not sent': 'The answer was refused and its retry was not sent.'}\n   537\tFORMAT_INVALID = 'The answer did not match the required format.'\n   538\t\n   539\t\n   540\tdef packet_units(results, items):\n   541\t    \"\"\"Every packet the run gives, as (unit, arm, draw) -> (decision, per-card source): the joint and singleton answers from the finals,\n   542\t    the separate arm's reconciled pairs with each card's own separate answer.\"\"\"\n   543\t    units = {}\n   544\t    for key, entry in results['finals'].items():\n   545\t        unit, arm, draw = key.split('|')\n   546\t        if not arm.startswith('separate-'):\n   547\t            first = first_attempt(entry)                    # [47e.1] the first attempt is scored on both arms\n   548\t            units[(unit, arm, draw)] = (first.get('decision'), {v: first for v in items[(unit, arm)]['members']})\n   549\t    for key, entry in results['reconciled'].items():\n   550\t        unit, draw = key.split('|')\n   551\t        per_card = {a.split('-', 1)[1]: first_attempt(results['finals'].get(f'{unit}|{a}|{draw}', {})) for (u, a) in items\n   552\t                    if u == unit and a.startswith('separate-')}\n   553\t        units[(unit, 'separate', draw)] = (entry.get('decision'), per_card)\n   554\t    return units\n   555\t\n   556\t\n   557\tdef card_lines(base, fam, v, token, data, final_label, prefix=''):\n   558\t    \"\"\"One card's answer as a reader sees it: the passages it names, its own figures, its recomputed outcome and assumptions, the card.\n   559\t    Returns (lines, ids a ground may name).\"\"\"\n   560\t    if not data:\n   561\t        return [f'  {final_label}'], set()\n   562\t    fmt = base.get('format')\n   563\t    calc = decode(data, fmt, fam)\n   564\t    try:\n   565\t        checked = checker(fmt).check(fam, base['passages'], calc)\n   566\t    except Exception as error:\n   567\t        checked = {'errors': [('checker', str(error))], 'recorded': [], 'published': {}}\n   568\t    try:\n   569\t        norm, recorded, named = card_view(calc, v, checked.get('recorded', []), prefix, checker(fmt))\n   570\t    except StopIteration:\n   571\t        return ['  The answer has no card for this question.'], set()\n   572\t    lines = ['  Passages, as the request showed them:\\n' + '\\n'.join('  ' + base['shown'].get(e, f'- {e} (not shown)') for e in named),\n   573\t             '  Figures (declared):\\n' + '\\n'.join(f'  - {json.dumps(f, ensure_ascii=False)}' for f in norm['figures']),\n   574\t             '  Recomputed outcome: ' + json.dumps((checked.get('published') or {}).get(v)),\n   575\t             '  Recorded assumptions: ' + json.dumps(recorded),\n   576\t             f'  Card {token}: ' + json.dumps(norm['answers'][0], ensure_ascii=False)]\n   577\t    return lines, set(named) | {f['id'] for f in norm['figures']}\n   578\t\n   579\t\n   580\tdef packet_body(items, unit, arm, decision, per_card):\n   581\t    \"\"\"[47d.3, 47e.1] One scoring packet: each card's scored (first) answer only. No attempt history, no code decision and no check code,\n   582\t    which would tell separate calls from one joint call; the verdict applies the code's decision itself. Returns (lines, grounds, members).\"\"\"\n   583\t    base = items[(unit, 'joint' if unit.startswith('pair') else 'single')]\n   584\t    grounds, lines = set(), []\n   585\t    for number, v in enumerate(base['members'], 1):\n   586\t        q = base['questions'][v]\n   587\t        token = f'K{number}'\n   588\t        grounds.add(token)\n   589\t        lines.append(f'### Card {token}: {q[\"question\"]}\\n  Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {i + 1}: {c}' for i, c in enumerate(q['ladder'])))\n   590\t        source = per_card.get(v, {})                         # the scored (first) attempt of this card\n   591\t        label = NO_ANSWER.get(source.get('decision'), FORMAT_INVALID if source.get('status') == 'format invalid' else NO_ANSWER['not sent'])\n   592\t        fam = base['family'] if arm != 'separate' else only(base['family'], v)\n   593\t        body, named = card_lines(base, fam, v, token, source.get('data'), label)\n   594\t        lines += body\n   595\t        grounds |= named\n   596\t    lines.append('For each card answer yes or no, each with a ground that names a card (K...), passage (e...) or figure (F...) of this packet: '\n   597\t                 + '; '.join(f'{k}: {t}' for k, t in QUESTIONS.items()) + '\\n')\n   598\t    return lines, sorted(grounds), base['members']\n   599\t\n   600\t\n   601\tdef key_commitment(key):\n   602\t    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(key, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\n   603\t\n   604\t\n   605\tdef render_packets(out, key):\n   606\t    \"\"\"The scoring packets for a key {salt, run_digest, order}: the key's salted sha256 first (so the text the readers receive commits\n   607\t    to the mapping), then each packet in the key's order, rendered from the run's results and plan.\"\"\"\n   608\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   609\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   610\t    units = packet_units(results, items)\n   611\t    lines, rendered = [f'Key commitment: {key_commitment(key)}', ''], {}\n   612\t    for pid, unit_key in key['order']:\n   613\t        decision, per_card = units[tuple(unit_key)]\n   614\t        body, grounds, members = packet_body(items, unit_key[0], unit_key[1], decision, per_card)\n   615\t        lines += [f'## {pid}'] + body\n   616\t        rendered[pid] = {'unit': unit_key[0], 'arm': unit_key[1], 'draw': unit_key[2], 'decision': decision, 'grounds': grounds,\n   617\t                         'cards': {f'K{n}': v for n, v in enumerate(members, 1)}}\n   618\t    return '\\n'.join(lines), rendered, units\n   619\t\n   620\t\n   621\tdef returned_text(raw):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && { nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '638,890p'; nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '252,285p'; }\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && { nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '638,890p'; nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '252,285p'; }\"","aggregated_output":"   638\tdef render_attempts(out, labels):\n   639\t    \"\"\"[47d.3, 47e.3] For diagnostic reading only, never scored: every retry and every returned text that failed the format check, each\n   640\t    under its own shuffled label (D01..), with the question, that attempt's own answer (or the text returned and the passages it names),\n   641\t    and no link to a packet.\"\"\"\n   642\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   643\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   644\t    lines = []\n   645\t    for label, (unit, arm, draw, v, attempt) in labels:\n   646\t        entry = results['finals'][f'{unit}|{arm}|{draw}']\n   647\t        a = next(x for x in entry['attempts'] if x['attempt'] == attempt)\n   648\t        base = items[(unit, 'joint' if unit.startswith('pair') else 'single')]\n   649\t        fam = base['family'] if arm in ('joint', 'single') else only(base['family'], v)\n   650\t        lines.append(f'## {label}: {base[\"questions\"][v][\"question\"]}')\n   651\t        if a.get('status') == 'format invalid':\n   652\t            returned = returned_text(a.get('raw'))\n   653\t            named = sorted(set(re.findall(r'\\be\\d+\\b', returned)) & set(base['shown']))\n   654\t            lines.append(f'  {FORMAT_INVALID} The text returned:\\n' + '\\n'.join('    ' + l for l in returned.splitlines()))\n   655\t            if named:\n   656\t                lines.append('  Passages it names, as the request showed them:\\n' + '\\n'.join('  ' + base['shown'][e] for e in named))\n   657\t            continue\n   658\t        lines += card_lines(base, fam, v, 'K1', a.get('data'), NO_ANSWER.get(a.get('decision'), NO_ANSWER['transport']), 'T.')[0]\n   659\t    return '\\n'.join(lines)\n   660\t\n   661\t\n   662\tdef packets(out, key_dir):\n   663\t    if (key_dir / 'packet-key.json').exists():            # [47b.4] the inventory and key are frozen once made\n   664\t        raise SystemExit(f'{key_dir / \"packet-key.json\"} exists: the packets are frozen; refused')\n   665\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   666\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   667\t    rng = random.Random(secrets.randbits(64))\n   668\t    unit_keys = sorted(packet_units(results, items))\n   669\t    rng.shuffle(unit_keys)\n   670\t    earlier = sorted((k.split('|')[0], k.split('|')[1], k.split('|')[2], v, a['attempt'])     # every retry, and every format failure\n   671\t                     for k, e in results['finals'].items() for a in (e.get('attempts') or [])\n   672\t                     if a['attempt'] >= 2 or a.get('status') == 'format invalid'\n   673\t                     for v in items[tuple(k.split('|')[:2])]['members'])\n   674\t    rng.shuffle(earlier)\n   675\t    key = {'salt': secrets.token_hex(16), 'run_digest': run_digest(out), 'order': [(f'P{n:02d}', list(u)) for n, u in enumerate(unit_keys, 1)],\n   676\t           'attempts': [(f'D{n:02d}', list(e)) for n, e in enumerate(earlier, 1)]}\n   677\t    text = render_packets(out, key)[0]\n   678\t    attempts_text = render_attempts(out, key['attempts'])          # [47f.2] both rendered before anything is written\n   679\t    if (out / 'packets.md').exists() or (out / 'attempts.md').exists():\n   680\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} already holds packets; refused')\n   681\t    key_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   682\t    with open(key_dir / 'packet-key.json', 'x') as handle:\n   683\t        json.dump(key, handle, indent=1)\n   684\t    with open(out / 'packets.md', 'x') as handle:\n   685\t        handle.write(text)\n   686\t    with open(out / 'attempts.md', 'x') as handle:\n   687\t        handle.write(attempts_text)\n   688\t    print(f'{len(key[\"order\"])} packets, {len(key[\"attempts\"])} diagnostic attempts; key in {key_dir}')\n   689\t\n   690\t\n   691\tdef _grounded(ground, grounds):\n   692\t    \"\"\"[47b.4] A ground is non-empty text that names at least one card, passage or figure of the packet.\"\"\"\n   693\t    return isinstance(ground, str) and ground.strip() != '' and any(re.search(rf'\\b{re.escape(g)}\\b', ground) for g in grounds)\n   694\t\n   695\t\n   696\tdef final_readings(pid, cards, members, grounds=()):\n   697\t    \"\"\"[47.4] Two independent readings per card (A, B), each question answered yes/no with its ground; a third decides each\n   698\t    disagreement. Returns ({card: {question: answer}}, problems).\"\"\"\n   699\t    problems, final = [], {}\n   700\t    if sorted(cards) != sorted(members):\n   701\t        return None, [f'{pid}: cards {sorted(cards)} are not the unit\\'s {sorted(members)}']\n   702\t    for v, r in cards.items():\n   703\t        final[v] = {}\n   704\t        for q in QUESTIONS:\n   705\t            a, b = (r.get(x, {}).get(q, {}) for x in ('A', 'B'))\n   706\t            for name, x in (('A', a), ('B', b)):\n   707\t                if x.get('answer') not in ('yes', 'no') or not _grounded(x.get('ground'), grounds):\n   708\t                    problems.append(f'{pid} {v} {q}: reader {name} gave no yes/no with a ground from this packet')\n   709\t            if a.get('answer') == b.get('answer'):\n   710\t                final[v][q] = a.get('answer')\n   711\t            else:\n   712\t                t = r.get('third', {}).get(q, {})\n   713\t                if t.get('answer') not in ('yes', 'no') or not _grounded(t.get('ground'), grounds):\n   714\t                    problems.append(f'{pid} {v} {q}: the readers disagree and no third reading decides')\n   715\t                final[v][q] = t.get('answer')\n   716\t    return final, problems\n   717\t\n   718\t\n   719\tdef verdict(out, readings_path, key_dir):\n   720\t    \"\"\"[47e.4] Seal the readings into the run (readings.json, created once), compute D725's lines once and write verdict.json bound to\n   721\t    the readings, the key and the packets. A second verdict on the run is refused; `replay` recomputes and compares.\"\"\"\n   722\t    if (out / 'verdict.json').exists() or (out / 'readings.json').exists():\n   723\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} already has sealed readings or a verdict; refused (use replay)')\n   724\t    data = Path(readings_path).read_bytes()\n   725\t    with open(out / 'readings.json', 'xb') as handle:\n   726\t        handle.write(data)\n   727\t    summary = score(out, key_dir)\n   728\t    frozen = json.loads((key_dir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   729\t    record = {'readings_sha256': hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), 'key_commitment': key_commitment(frozen),\n   730\t              'packets_sha256': hashlib.sha256((out / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest() if (out / 'packets.md').exists() else None,\n   731\t              'run_digest': run_digest(out), 'summary': summary}\n   732\t    with open(out / 'verdict.json', 'x') as handle:\n   733\t        json.dump(record, handle, indent=1)\n   734\t    return summary\n   735\t\n   736\t\n   737\tdef replay(out, key_dir):\n   738\t    \"\"\"Recompute the verdict from the sealed readings and compare it with verdict.json.\"\"\"\n   739\t    record = json.loads((out / 'verdict.json').read_text())\n   740\t    data = (out / 'readings.json').read_bytes()\n   741\t    same = (hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest() == record['readings_sha256'] and record['run_digest'] == run_digest(out)\n   742\t            and record['key_commitment'] == key_commitment(json.loads((key_dir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())))\n   743\t    summary = score(out, key_dir)\n   744\t    matches = same and summary == record['summary']\n   745\t    print(json.dumps({'reproduced': matches}, indent=1))\n   746\t    return matches\n   747\t\n   748\t\n   749\tdef score(out, key_dir):\n   750\t    \"\"\"D725's registered lines on the sealed readings, bound to this run.\"\"\"\n   751\t    frozen = json.loads((key_dir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   752\t    submitted = json.loads((out / 'readings.json').read_text())\n   753\t    problems = [] if frozen.get('run_digest') == run_digest(out) else ['the packet key does not belong to this run']   # [47b.4]\n   754\t    text, key, units = render_packets(out, frozen)                  # [47c.2] every packet rendered again from the run\n   755\t    if sorted(tuple(u) for _, u in frozen['order']) != sorted(units):\n   756\t        problems.append('the key does not map one packet to each unit of the run')\n   757\t    sha = hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()\n   758\t    packets_path = out / 'packets.md'\n   759\t    written = packets_path.read_text() if packets_path.exists() else ''\n   760\t    if not written.startswith(f'Key commitment: {key_commitment(frozen)}\\n'):      # [47d.1] the mapping the readers' text committed to\n   761\t        problems.append('the key is not the one packets.md committed to')\n   762\t    if hashlib.sha256(written.encode()).hexdigest() != sha:\n   763\t        problems.append('packets.md is not the text the run and the key give')\n   764\t    if submitted.get('packets_sha256') != sha:\n   765\t        problems.append('the readings were not made on the frozen packets')\n   766\t    readings = submitted.get('packets', {})\n   767\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   768\t    problems += [f'answers.jsonl line {d[\"line\"]} is damaged' for d in results.get('damaged', [])\n   769\t                 if d.get('journal') == 'answers.jsonl']                     # [47g] a damaged retry record stays diagnostic\n   770\t    scored = {k: first_attempt(v)['decision'] for k, v in results['finals'].items()}            # [47f.1] completeness from the scored attempts\n   771\t    problems += [f'{k}: {d}' for k, d in scored.items() if d not in ('publish', 'held', 'refused')]               # [47b.2] from the records\n   772\t    problems += [f'{pid}: not read' for pid in key if pid not in readings] + [f'{pid}: not a packet' for pid in readings if pid not in key]\n   773\t    usable_pairs = {'joint': {}, 'separate': {}}\n   774\t    defects = []\n   775\t    for pid, k in key.items():\n   776\t        if pid not in readings:\n   777\t            continue\n   778\t        final, probs = final_readings(pid, readings[pid], list(k['cards']), k['grounds'])\n   779\t        problems += probs\n   780\t        if final is None:\n   781\t            continue\n   782\t        if k['decision'] == 'publish' and k['arm'] in ('joint', 'single'):      # D725: defects across the joint and singleton answers\n   783\t            for v, r in final.items():\n   784\t                if 'yes' in (r['contradiction'], r['internal_reference'], r['deciding_gap']):\n   785\t                    defects.append((pid, k['unit'], k['arm'], k['cards'][v]))\n   786\t        if k['unit'].startswith('pair') and k['arm'] in usable_pairs:\n   787\t            usable_pairs[k['arm']].setdefault(k['unit'], []).append(k['decision'] == 'publish' and all(r['usable'] == 'yes' for r in final.values()))\n   788\t    joint_total = sum(sum(v) for v in usable_pairs['joint'].values())\n   789\t    separate_total = sum(sum(v) for v in usable_pairs['separate'].values())\n   790\t    per_snapshot = {u: sum(v) for u, v in usable_pairs['joint'].items()}\n   791\t    complete = (not problems and len(key) == 27 and len(usable_pairs['joint']) == 3 and len(usable_pairs['separate']) == 3\n   792\t                and all(len(v) == 3 for arm in usable_pairs.values() for v in arm.values()))\n   793\t    passes = complete and not defects and joint_total >= 8 and all(n >= 2 for n in per_snapshot.values()) and joint_total - separate_total >= 3\n   794\t    summary = {'complete': complete, 'problems': problems[:20], 'joint usable pairs': joint_total, 'separate usable pairs': separate_total,\n   795\t               'joint per snapshot': per_snapshot, 'published defects': defects,\n   796\t               'verdict': 'PASS' if passes else ('INCOMPLETE' if not complete else 'STOP')}\n   797\t    print(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))\n   798\t    return summary\n   799\t\n   800\t\n   801\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   802\t    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ''\n   803\t    if cmd == 'plan' and len(sys.argv) == 3:\n   804\t        plan(sys.argv[2])\n   805\t    elif cmd == 'plan-v13s' and len(sys.argv) == 3:                     # D737: the small format's plan, $0\n   806\t        plan(sys.argv[2], 'v13s')\n   807\t    elif cmd == 'send' and len(sys.argv) == 5 and not sys.argv[2].startswith('-'):\n   808\t        send(Path(sys.argv[2]), float(sys.argv[3]), sys.argv[4])\n   809\t    elif cmd == 'packets' and len(sys.argv) == 4:\n   810\t        packets(Path(sys.argv[2]), Path(sys.argv[3]))\n   811\t    elif cmd == 'recover' and len(sys.argv) == 3:\n   812\t        recover(Path(sys.argv[2]))\n   813\t    elif cmd == 'verdict' and len(sys.argv) == 5:\n   814\t        verdict(Path(sys.argv[2]), sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4]))\n   815\t    elif cmd == 'replay' and len(sys.argv) == 4:\n   816\t        replay(Path(sys.argv[2]), Path(sys.argv[3]))\n   817\t    else:\n   818\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n   252\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   276\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   277\t\n   278\t## 5. What the result decides\n   279\t\n   280\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   281\t  step Alex opens.\n   282\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
