{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && { nl -ba small-rehearsal.log | tail -25; nl -ba small_rehearsal.py | tail -145; nl -ba BLIND7-RESULT.md | head -100; rg -n 'refus|replay|rate|guard|paid|INCOMPLETE' SMALL-DESIGN.md | tail -55; }\"","aggregated_output":"    37\t  \"single-O|single|1\": \"publish\",\n    38\t  \"single-O|single|2\": \"publish\",\n    39\t  \"single-O|single|3\": \"publish\",\n    40\t  \"single-S|single|1\": \"publish\",\n    41\t  \"single-S|single|2\": \"publish\",\n    42\t  \"single-S|single|3\": \"publish\",\n    43\t  \"single-E|single|1\": \"publish\",\n    44\t  \"single-E|single|2\": \"publish\",\n    45\t  \"single-E|single|3\": \"publish\"\n    46\t }\n    47\t}\n    48\tPASS  recovery rewrites results.json from the journals, identical\n    49\tPASS  the separate Data Center card alone publishes\n    50\tPASS  reconciliation refuses the pair for S3\n    51\tPASS  a joint answer with two company Q3 forecasts is refused on its first attempt (S4)\n    52\tPASS  its diagnostic retry publishes\n    53\tPASS  a rung outside the ladder is refused (S6)\n    54\tPASS  a misread source number is refused (S1) on the first attempt\n    55\tPASS  wrong arithmetic is refused (S2) on the first attempt\n    56\tPASS  an estimate marked as the market reference is refused (S5) on the first attempt\n    57\tPASS  Data Center added into total revenue is refused (S8) on the first attempt\n    58\tPASS  its correct counterpart, a real quoted amount read right, publishes\n    59\tPASS  the other draws of the same units publish\n    60\tPASS  the old v13 run reproduces results.json byte for byte from its journals (ledger snapshot from results.json)\n    61\t19 of 19 checks pass\n   101\t        figures.append(both)\n   102\t    for f in figures:\n   103\t        f.setdefault('outcome_for', [])\n   104\t        f.setdefault('reference_for', [])\n   105\t    return {'figures': figures, 'answers': answers}\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef pid_text(it, p):\n   109\t    return p\n   110\t\n   111\t\n   112\tclass Stub:\n   113\t    def __init__(self, cfg, scenario):\n   114\t        self.cfg, self.scenario, self.problems, self.sent, self.draws = cfg, scenario, [], 0, {}\n   115\t\n   116\t    def expected(self, it, user):\n   117\t        s = self.cfg.rejudging\n   118\t        return json.dumps({'model': s.model, 'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': it['system']}, {'role': 'user', 'content': user}],\n   119\t                           'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'name': 'judgement', 'strict': True, 'schema': it['schema']}},\n   120\t                           'max_completion_tokens': s.max_output_tokens, 'reasoning_effort': s.reasoning_effort}).encode('utf-8')\n   121\t\n   122\t    def __call__(self, http_request, *args, **kwargs):\n   123\t        body = http_request.data\n   124\t        user = json.loads(body)['messages'][1]['content']\n   125\t        retry = pg.RETRY_MARK in user\n   126\t        it = BY_USER.get(user.split(pg.RETRY_MARK)[0])\n   127\t        if it is None or body != self.expected(it, user):\n   128\t            self.problems.append('a body that is not the planned request, byte for byte')\n   129\t            raise urllib.error.HTTPError(http_request.full_url, 400, 'bad', {}, io.BytesIO(b'{}'))\n   130\t        self.sent += 1\n   131\t        flavour = 'ok'\n   132\t        if self.scenario == 'separate-contradiction' and it['arm'] == 'separate-v9':\n   133\t            flavour = 'dc-high'\n   134\t        if self.scenario == 'joint-defects' and it['unit'] == 'pair-old-2' and it['arm'] == 'joint' and not retry:\n   135\t            flavour = 'two-q3'\n   136\t        if self.scenario == 'joint-defects' and it['unit'] == 'single-E' and not retry:\n   137\t            flavour = 'bad-rung'\n   138\t        if self.scenario == 'named-defects' and not retry:          # [54] a defective and a correct answer for each named defect\n   139\t            draw = self.draws.setdefault(key := (it['unit'], it['arm']), 0) + 1\n   140\t            self.draws[key] = draw\n   141\t            flavour = {('single-O', 1): 'src-misread', ('single-O', 2): 'src-ok', ('single-O', 3): 'arith',\n   142\t                       ('single-S', 1): 'ref-est', ('pair-old-1', 1): 'dc-into-total'}.get((it['unit'], draw), 'ok') \\\n   143\t                if it['arm'] in ('single', 'joint') else 'ok'\n   144\t        usage = {'prompt_tokens': len(body) // 4, 'completion_tokens': 800}\n   145\t        return FakeResponse(json.dumps({'choices': [{'message': {'content': json.dumps(answer(it, flavour))}}], 'usage': usage}).encode('utf-8'))\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\tdef scenario(scratch, name):\n   149\t    out = scratch / name\n   150\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n   151\t    budget = pg.budget_module()\n   152\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(out / 'ledger.json'), 0.5)\n   153\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(out / 'ledger.json'))\n   154\t    gate = pg.Gate(out, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger, sleep=lambda seconds: None), ledger)\n   155\t    (out / 'plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(PLAN))\n   156\t    stub = Stub(gate.cfg, name)\n   157\t    saved = (urllib.request.urlopen, os.environ.get('OPENAI_API_KEY'))\n   158\t    os.environ['OPENAI_API_KEY'] = 'rehearsal-dummy-not-a-key'\n   159\t    urllib.request.urlopen = stub\n   160\t    remove_gate = budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   161\t    try:\n   162\t        summary = gate.run(PLAN)\n   163\t    finally:\n   164\t        remove_gate()\n   165\t        urllib.request.urlopen = saved[0]\n   166\t        if saved[1] is None:\n   167\t            os.environ.pop('OPENAI_API_KEY', None)\n   168\t        else:\n   169\t            os.environ['OPENAI_API_KEY'] = saved[1]\n   170\t    return out, summary, stub\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\tdef main(scratch):\n   174\t    scratch = Path(scratch)\n   175\t    if scratch.exists():\n   176\t        raise SystemExit(f'{scratch} exists')\n   177\t    checks = []\n   178\t\n   179\t    def ok(name, cond, detail=''):\n   180\t        checks.append(cond)\n   181\t        print(f'{\"PASS\" if cond else \"FAIL\"}  {name}' + ('' if cond else f'  {detail}'))\n   182\t\n   183\t    out, summary, stub = scenario(scratch, 'ok')\n   184\t    ok('every request is the planned v13s body, byte for byte', not stub.problems, stub.problems)\n   185\t    ok('36 first attempts sent, none refused', stub.sent == 36, stub.sent)\n   186\t    decisions = {k: v['decision'] for k, v in summary['finals'].items()}\n   187\t    ok('every first attempt publishes', set(decisions.values()) == {'publish'}, decisions)\n   188\t    rec = {k: v['decision'] for k, v in summary['reconciled'].items()}\n   189\t    ok('every separate pair reconciles and publishes', set(rec.values()) == {'publish'}, rec)\n   190\t    joint = next(i for i in PLAN if i['arm'] == 'joint')\n   191\t    data = summary['finals'][f'{joint[\"unit\"]}|joint|1']['data']\n   192\t    lines, grounds = pg.card_lines(joint, joint['family'], joint['members'][0], 'K1', data, 'no answer')\n   193\t    text = '\\n'.join(lines)\n   194\t    ok('the reader card shows a recomputed outcome', 'Recomputed outcome: [' in text, text[:600])\n   195\t    ok('the reader card maps the recorded estimate to the card\\'s figure numbers', '\"type\": \"estimate\", \"figure\": \"F' in text, text[:900])\n   196\t    before = (out / 'results.json').read_bytes()\n   197\t    pg.recover(out)\n   198\t    ok('recovery rewrites results.json from the journals, identical', (out / 'results.json').read_bytes() == before)\n   199\t\n   200\t    out, summary, stub = scenario(scratch, 'separate-contradiction')\n   201\t    rec = summary['reconciled']\n   202\t    first = {k: v['decision'] for k, v in summary['finals'].items() if 'separate-v9' in k and 'pair-old-2' in k}\n   203\t    ok('the separate Data Center card alone publishes', set(first.values()) == {'publish'}, first)\n   204\t    ok('reconciliation refuses the pair for S3', all(rec[f'pair-old-2|{d}']['decision'] == 'refused' and\n   205\t                                                      any(e[0] == 'S3' for e in rec[f'pair-old-2|{d}']['errors']) for d in pg.DRAWS),\n   206\t       {d: rec[f'pair-old-2|{d}'] for d in pg.DRAWS})\n   207\t\n   208\t    out, summary, stub = scenario(scratch, 'joint-defects')\n   209\t    fin = summary['finals']\n   210\t    two = fin['pair-old-2|joint|1']\n   211\t    ok('a joint answer with two company Q3 forecasts is refused on its first attempt (S4)', two['attempts'][0]['decision'] == 'refused'\n   212\t       and any(e[0] == 'S4' for e in two['attempts'][0]['errors']), two['attempts'][0].get('errors'))\n   213\t    ok('its diagnostic retry publishes', two['attempts'][-1]['decision'] == 'publish', two['attempts'][-1].get('decision'))\n   214\t    e = fin['single-E|single|1']['attempts'][0]\n   215\t    ok('a rung outside the ladder is refused (S6)', e['decision'] == 'refused' and any(x[0] == 'S6' for x in e['errors']), e.get('errors'))\n   216\t\n   217\t    out, summary, stub = scenario(scratch, 'named-defects')\n   218\t    fin = summary['finals']\n   219\t\n   220\t    def first(key):\n   221\t        return fin[key]['attempts'][0]\n   222\t    for key, rule, label in (('single-O|single|1', 'S1', 'a misread source number'), ('single-O|single|3', 'S2', 'wrong arithmetic'),\n   223\t                             ('single-S|single|1', 'S5', 'an estimate marked as the market reference'),\n   224\t                             ('pair-old-1|joint|1', 'S8', 'Data Center added into total revenue')):\n   225\t        a = first(key)\n   226\t        ok(f'{label} is refused ({rule}) on the first attempt', a['decision'] == 'refused' and {e[0] for e in a['errors']} == {rule}, a.get('errors'))\n   227\t    a = first('single-O|single|2')\n   228\t    ok('its correct counterpart, a real quoted amount read right, publishes', a['decision'] == 'publish', a.get('errors'))\n   229\t    ok('the other draws of the same units publish', all(first(f'pair-old-1|joint|{d}')['decision'] == 'publish' for d in (2, 3))\n   230\t       and all(first(f'single-S|single|{d}')['decision'] == 'publish' for d in (2, 3)))\n   231\t\n   232\t    copy = scratch / 'old-run-copy'\n   233\t    shutil.copytree(OLD_RUN, copy, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('archives'))\n   234\t    saved = json.loads((copy / 'results.json').read_text())\n   235\t    items = json.loads((copy / 'plan.json').read_text())\n   236\t    original = (copy / 'results.json').read_bytes()\n   237\t    pg.summarise(copy, items, saved['ledger'])\n   238\t    ok('the old v13 run reproduces results.json byte for byte from its journals (ledger snapshot from results.json)',\n   239\t       (copy / 'results.json').read_bytes() == original)\n   240\t    print(f'{sum(checks)} of {len(checks)} checks pass')\n   241\t    return 0 if all(checks) else 1\n   242\t\n   243\t\n   244\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   245\t    raise SystemExit(main(sys.argv[1]))\n     1\t# The D751 last writer test of the wording loop: result\n     2\t\n     3\tRun folder: `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/`. It was registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D751] and scored by\n     4\t`blind7.py tally` (`TALLY.json`, `reasons.json`). The request is `judging-v13s.txt`, sha256 `080a0012…`.\n     5\t\n     6\t## 1. Verdict: FAIL on one settled line, so the exit rule applies\n     7\t\n     8\t| Packet | Answer | Shape, rung | First readers (Codex, Claude) | Adjudicators (Codex, Claude) | Settled | Line |\n     9\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    10\t| X01 | fresh E Claude | forecast, rung 3 ($37B: 85% growth) | no, no | (none) | **no** | **FAIL** |\n    11\t| X06 | fresh E Codex | unresolved | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    12\t| X07 | fresh S Codex | forecast, rung 4 ($745B − $25B = $720B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    13\t| X03 | fresh S Claude | forecast, rung 4 ($730B − $20B = $710B) | no, yes | no, yes | split | inconclusive |\n    14\t| X04 | fresh P-v8 Claude | forecast, rung 2 ($383.9B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    15\t| X05 | fresh P-v8 Codex | forecast, rung 2 ($375.8B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    16\t| X02 | control: invented cut | forecast | no, no | (none) | no | ok |\n    17\t| X08 | control: impossible floor | forecast | floor marked by Codex only | floor upheld by both | floor settled | ok |\n    18\t\n    19\t- **The failure.** X01 placed 85% growth \"about 70% of the way\" between the market pace and \"more than double\". Both readers:\n    20\t  - the 85% is an interpolation;\n    21\t  - no passage sizes a shortfall;\n    22\t  - the market pace bounds only the rung 3/4 line;\n    23\t  - \"more than double\" is a floor.\n    24\t- **The split.** X03's $20B deduction rests on outside data-center totals that do not name the four companies, and on Amazon as the\n    25\t  only material non-data-center programme. Codex says this does not show the deduction stays at or under $30B. Claude accepts it as\n    26\t  an explained related figure.\n    27\t- **The exit rule** (council 67, registered in [D751]): a settled failure ends this wording loop, and the publication choice for\n    28\t  E-type cases returns to Alex.\n    29\t\n    30\t## 2. The record across the five runs (same cases, same passages)\n    31\t\n    32\t| Case | Codex writer | Claude writer |\n    33\t|---|---|---|\n    34\t| E | 2 invented cuts (no), then 3 justified \"unresolved\" (yes, yes, yes) | 5 forecasts by five routes ($37B, $32.4B, $42B, $35B, $37B): never settled supported (no, no, split, no, no; the first was accepted in one reading and split in another) |\n    35\t| S | D749 supported; D750 supported; D751 supported | D749 split; D750 supported, with two defect splits; D751 split |\n    36\t| P-v8 | supported every run | supported every run |\n    37\t| Controls | caught in every run since D749 (6 of 6) | |\n    38\t\n    39\t- **The request's repairs (D749–D751)** turned the Codex writer from inventing cuts to naming the missing fact. They did not move\n    40\t  the Claude writer, whose answers on boundary cases readers either reject (E) or split on (S).\n    41\t- **The writers are proxies.** The production model is luna, and only the paid re-send measures it.\n    42\t\n    43\t## 3. Not done\n    44\t\n    45\tNothing was paid. Nothing was tuned on the 36 stored answers. The request was not changed after the registration.\n1:# judging-v13 small format (v13s): code refuses only the five defects and broken structure (D737)\n3:Alex (D737) chose to shrink the format. Code refuses an answer only for these five defects:\n10:It also refuses broken structure. Each rule is written in one or two sentences beside its field. Every other rule of `DESIGN.md`'s\n11:checks becomes something the readers see, not a refusal.\n43:| S2 | wrong arithmetic | A computed figure equals its operation's result within 0.5% (at least 0.1, or 0.05 for %). Units are those `operation` states for each operation; a sum or difference adds one unit. A range input gives a range: both extremes are computed first, and a midpoint may be declared as value. Division by a range that contains zero is refused. | `operation` |\n57:- apply_growth(base, rate %): base's unit.\n72:**Recorded for readers, never refused:**\n88:| `operation` | \"Computed only. sum(a, b, …) = a + b + … (one unit); difference(a, b) = a − b (one unit); product(a, b, …) = a × b × … (USD bn × x, x × x or % × x; never USD bn × %); ratio(a, b) = a ÷ b (same units give x; USD bn ÷ x gives USD bn); share(whole, percent) = whole × percent ÷ 100; growth(old, new) = the % change; apply_growth(base, rate %) = base × (1 + rate ÷ 100). sum and product take two or more inputs; the others exactly two. A range input gives a range: compute both extremes; you may declare the midpoint as value. The figure equals the result within 0.5% (at least 0.1, or 0.05 for %). A sum never adds a figure built on the part's quantity to one built on the whole's (the whole already includes the part); a difference may take the part from the whole only to give the rest. When its inputs are periods of one quantity, write them FY2027, FY2027 Q3, FY2027 H1 or FY2027 Q1-Q3 (or CY likewise), and they make up the output's period exactly (Q1 + Q2 = H1; FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4).\" |\n118:| `operation` | enum sum, difference, product, ratio, share, growth, apply_growth; or null | \"Computed only. sum(a, b, …) = a + b + …; difference(a, b) = a − b; product(a, b, …) = a × b × …, never money by a percentage; ratio(a, b) = a ÷ b; share(whole, percent) = whole × percent ÷ 100; growth(old, new) = the % change from old to new; apply_growth(base, rate) = base × (1 + rate ÷ 100). difference, ratio, share, growth and apply_growth take exactly two inputs. A range input gives a range (low and high, or their midpoint as value). The figure equals the result within 0.5% (at least 0.1, or 0.05 for %). A sum or difference never combines the part's quantity with the whole's; when its inputs are periods of one quantity, they make up the output's period exactly (Q1 + Q2 = H1; FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4).\" |\n148:- **The plan.** `paid_gate.item` takes a format. A v13s plan (`paid-plan-v13s.json`, pinned) uses `calc_small`. A plan without a\n160:**State × event:** unchanged from D731. A refusal is retried once, diagnostic only; the first attempt is scored.\n164:**Inputs.** Each case's archive, call, question, ladder and unit are registered, and the build refuses a heading that differs.\n168:| P (joint), P-v4, P-v8 (separate) | old-1 v4 8810, v8 8816 | NVIDIA revenue company FY2027; NVIDIA revenue Data Center FY2027 | 431.2/392/352.8/313.6; 400/350/300/250 | the pair; 79 quotes absent from the gate |\n179:  - a year-over-year rate on last year's quarter (recorded);\n192:- **A2, defects.** Each is refused by its named rule:\n204:- **A3, Luna's observed mistakes** from both journals, each encoded in v13s. Each is impossible under the schema or refused with a\n224:  - an estimate resting on both part and whole (recorded, not refused, and the record asserted);\n238:- **A3:** each mistake must be refused by the schema or **actually refused** by its stated rule (asserted). \"first half\" is refused by\n240:- **A4, the end to end rehearsal.** One v13s reply goes through the first attempt, the separate-arm reconciliation, the card render and\n250:- **The wording review is separate.** Refusals are revealed only after that marking, for the review of whether the request states\n253:- **INCOMPLETE** is judged against the inventory of 12 first replies and 24 readings plus the third readings due.\n260:  answer, accepted or refused, against the shown passages. For each answer they record:\n261:  - for each refusal, whether the exact request states the condition (the sentence quoted) and whether the answer was right;\n268:- an A1 form refused;\n269:- an A2 defect not refused by its rule;\n271:- a Part B refusal whose condition the request does not state, or that refuses a right answer;\n272:- an INCOMPLETE run;\n276:**A clean result** goes to Alex as the request for the paid re-send: the same 36 requests rebuilt in v13s, under a new decision with\n279:**[D742] Registered before the third run (council rounds 56–56c).** The re-run stopped on one S4 refusal of a sound answer\n281:guidance rate only as \"a stated benchmark for an estimate\" and the header required every path to go through the forecast. S4 is\n286:- **The refusal review** records two judgements apart for each refusal:\n289:  A sound answer refused under a clearly stated condition still stops the run.\n290:- **The readers' brief** keeps Alex's ruling-1 sentence and adds: \"Look through any rate or multiple, including inside a stated\n298:  - a fresh sound refusal sends the format back to council;\n300:  - only a complete run that meets every line goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\n302:  - five new cases: the stated-estimate benchmark passes; four forms of the saved refusal or a guidance reset are refused by S4;\n304:  - `s4_replay.py` on the saved reply.\n323:  - A clean re-read goes to Alex for the paid re-send, beside the third run's record and its disclosures.\n348:  - A clean result goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\n379:  - the refusal and defect stop lines hold as before.\n383:  - a clean result supports asking Alex to authorize the 36-request paid re-send.\n418:  - The tally refuses a key that is not exactly the nine answers, or a reading without a valid vote. A settled vote is final only\n436:    $0 writer test, then Alex for the paid re-send.\n461:  - Checks at $0: cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, and the pinned v13 plan unchanged (`paid-plan.sha256`). The schema and the code\n488:    - a fresh reply refused or held by the code (decided before any reading; an unreadable reply builds no packet);\n497:  - Either outcome goes back to the council, and the paid re-send stays on hold.\n498:  - Only a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send.\n534:  - a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send;\n581:  - a clean pass goes to Alex for the paid authorization;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
