{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba calc_small.py | sed -n '1,107p;161,212p;772,797p'; nl -ba render_v13.py | sed -n '1,100p'; nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '336,414p'; nl -ba assemble_readings.py | head -130\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"judging-v13s checks: the small format (SMALL-DESIGN.md §2 [52] and [54], D737, D738). Harness-only. Code refuses an answer only for\n     2\tthe five named defects (S1 a number misread, S2 wrong arithmetic, S3/S8 a part above its whole or added into it, S4 two forecasts of one\n     3\tquarter, S5 an own estimate passed off as the market's) and for broken structure (S6, S7), and only where the calculation's own\n     4\tstructure decides it (D738). Everything else is recorded for readers.\n     5\t\n     6\tfrom_answer(data, family) -> the internal shape the harness reads ({'figures', 'answers', 'decode_errors'})\n     7\tcheck(family, passages, calc) -> {'errors': [(rule, detail)], 'recorded': [...], 'published': {view_id: [low, high, None]}}\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\timport itertools\n    10\timport math\n    11\timport re\n    12\t\n    13\tKINDS = {'source', 'computed', 'estimate'}\n    14\tBASES = {'reported', 'guidance', 'consensus', 'third_party', 'forecast'}\n    15\tEXTERNAL = {'consensus', 'guidance', 'third_party'}\n    16\tUNITS = {'USD bn', '%', 'x'}\n    17\tARITY = {'sum': (2, None), 'product': (2, None), 'difference': (2, 2), 'ratio': (2, 2), 'share': (2, 2), 'growth': (2, 2),\n    18\t         'apply_growth': (2, 2)}\n    19\tQUALIFIERS_BEFORE = sorted(['more than', 'at least', 'up to', 'as much as', 'less than', 'over', 'about', 'approximately', 'around',\n    20\t                            'roughly', 'nearly', 'almost', 'below', 'under', 'near', 'estimated'], key=len, reverse=True)\n    21\tQUALIFIERS_AFTER = ['or more', 'or less']\n    22\tQUALIFIERS = ['none'] + QUALIFIERS_BEFORE + QUALIFIERS_AFTER\n    23\tSCALE = {'trillion': 1000.0, 'tn': 1000.0, 't': 1000.0, 'billion': 1.0, 'bn': 1.0, 'b': 1.0, 'million': 0.001, 'mn': 0.001, 'm': 0.001}\n    24\tLIMIT = 1e9                                              # [54] a number beyond this is refused, not computed\n    25\tMAX_RANGE_LEAVES = 12\n    26\t\n    27\t_NUM = r'(\\d[\\d,]*(?:\\.\\d+)?)'\n    28\t_CUR = r'(?:US)?\\$\\s?'\n    29\t_SC = r'(?:\\s*(trillion|billion|million|bn|tn|mn|t|b|m)\\b)?'\n    30\t_MINUS = r'([-−–]\\s?)?'\n    31\t_PCT = r'\\s*(?:%|percent)'\n    32\t_BODIES = [   # [54] the complete numeric expressions, longest forms first; a quote_number must be one of them, whole\n    33\t    ('relative', _CUR + _NUM + _SC + r'\\s*,?\\s*\\(?\\s*(?:plus or minus|\\+/-|±)\\s*' + _NUM + r'\\s*%\\s*\\)?'),\n    34\t    ('range', _CUR + _NUM + _SC + r'\\s*(?:–|—|-|to)\\s*(?:' + _CUR + r')?' + _NUM + _SC),\n    35\t    ('range', r'between\\s+' + _CUR + _NUM + _SC + r'\\s+and\\s+(?:' + _CUR + r')?' + _NUM + _SC),\n    36\t    ('percent_range', r'between\\s+' + _NUM + r'\\s*%?\\s+and\\s+' + _NUM + _PCT),\n    37\t    ('percent_range', _NUM + r'\\s*%?\\s*(?:–|—|-|to)\\s*' + _NUM + _PCT),\n    38\t    ('money', _MINUS + _CUR + _NUM + _SC),\n    39\t    ('percent', _MINUS + _NUM + _PCT),\n    40\t    ('multiple', r'(double|triple|twice)'),\n    41\t]\n    42\t_ANCHORED = [(form, re.compile(r'^' + body + r'$', re.I)) for form, body in _BODIES]\n    43\t_SCAN = [(form, re.compile(r'(?<![\\w.,$])' + body + r'(?![\\w%])', re.I)) for form, body in _BODIES]\n    44\t_PERIOD = re.compile(r'^(FY|CY)(\\d{4})(?:\\s+(Q[1-4](?:-Q[1-4])?|H[12]))?$')\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef _num(text):\n    48\t    return float(text.replace(',', ''))\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef _money(number, scale):\n    52\t    return _num(number) * SCALE[scale.lower()] if scale else _num(number) / 1e9      # an amount with no scale is in dollars\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef parse_number(text):\n    56\t    \"\"\"A quote_number as written: {'unit', 'value'} or {'unit', 'low', 'high'[, 'mid']}; None when it is not one complete form.\"\"\"\n    57\t    text = (text or '').strip()\n    58\t    for form, pattern in _ANCHORED:\n    59\t        m = pattern.match(text)\n    60\t        if not m:\n    61\t            continue\n    62\t        g = m.groups()\n    63\t        if form == 'relative':\n    64\t            mid, rel = _money(g[0], g[1]), _num(g[2])\n    65\t            return {'unit': 'USD bn', 'low': mid * (1 - rel / 100), 'high': mid * (1 + rel / 100), 'mid': mid}\n    66\t        if form == 'range':\n    67\t            if not (g[1] or g[3]):\n    68\t                return None\n    69\t            return {'unit': 'USD bn', 'low': _money(g[0], g[1] or g[3]), 'high': _money(g[2], g[3] or g[1])}\n    70\t        if form == 'percent_range':\n    71\t            return {'unit': '%', 'low': _num(g[0]), 'high': _num(g[1])}\n    72\t        if form == 'money':\n    73\t            return {'unit': 'USD bn', 'value': (-1.0 if g[0] else 1.0) * _money(g[1], g[2])}\n    74\t        if form == 'percent':\n    75\t            return {'unit': '%', 'value': (-1.0 if g[0] else 1.0) * _num(g[1])}\n    76\t        return {'unit': 'x', 'value': 3.0 if g[0].lower() == 'triple' else 2.0}\n    77\t    return None\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t_CHANGE = re.compile(r'(?<!rang)(?<!range)(?<!ranges)(?<!ranging)\\bfrom\\s*$', re.I)\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef expressions(text):\n    84\t    \"\"\"[54] Every complete numeric expression in a quote, as (start, end), longest forms first and never overlapping. [D740] An\n    85\t    'X to Y' written after 'from' (not 'range(s) from' or 'ranging from') is a change between two values, so its two amounts are\n    86\t    separate expressions.\"\"\"\n    87\t    taken = []\n    88\t    for form, pattern in _SCAN:\n    89\t        for m in pattern.finditer(text):\n    90\t            if form == 'range' and re.search(r'\\bto\\b', m.group(0), re.I) and not m.group(0).lower().startswith('between'):\n    91\t                before = text[:m.start()].rstrip().lower()\n    92\t                if before.endswith('from') and not re.search(r'\\b(range|ranges|ranged|ranging)\\s+from$', before):\n    93\t                    continue\n    94\t            if not any(m.start() < e and s < m.end() for s, e in taken):\n    95\t                taken.append((m.start(), m.end()))\n    96\t    return sorted(taken)\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\tdef _key(what):\n   100\t    return (what['population'], what['measure'], what['scope'], what['period'])\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\tdef _quantity(what):\n   104\t    return (what['population'], what['measure'], what['scope'])\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\tdef _same(a, b):\n   161\t    \"\"\"The v13s wire answer as the internal shape: `evidence_id` becomes `evidence`; the markers become each answer's `outcome` and\n   162\t    `reference`; marker errors go in `decode_errors` (S5, S6, S7). An empty string counts as absent.\"\"\"\n   163\t    errors, figures, outcome_for, reference_for = [], [], {}, {}\n   164\t    members = family['members']\n   165\t    for f in data.get('figures') or []:\n   166\t        g = {k: f[k] for k in FIGURE_FIELDS if f.get(k) is not None}\n   167\t        if f.get('evidence_id') is not None:\n   168\t            g['evidence'] = f['evidence_id']\n   169\t        for marks, store in (('outcome_for', outcome_for), ('reference_for', reference_for)):\n   170\t            listed = f.get(marks) or []\n   171\t            for v in sorted(set(listed)):\n   172\t                if listed.count(v) > 1:\n   173\t                    errors.append(('S7', f'{f.get(\"id\")}: {marks} lists {v} more than once'))\n   174\t                store.setdefault(v, []).append(f.get('id'))\n   175\t        figures.append(g)\n   176\t    answers = []\n   177\t    for a in data.get('answers') or []:\n   178\t        v = a.get('view_id')\n   179\t        a2 = {k: a[k] for k in ('view_id', 'shape', 'rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'pushes', 'theme_pushes') if a.get(k) is not None}\n   180\t        if _text(a.get('why')):\n   181\t            a2['why'] = a['why']\n   182\t        if v not in members:\n   183\t            answers.append(a2)\n   184\t            continue\n   185\t        outs, refs, reason = outcome_for.get(v, []), reference_for.get(v, []), _text(a.get('reference_unavailable'))\n   186\t        if a.get('shape') == 'unresolved':\n   187\t            if outs or refs or reason or a.get('rung') is not None or not _text(a.get('why')):\n   188\t                errors.append(('S7', f'{v}: an unresolved answer has why, rung and reference_unavailable null, and no figure marked for it'))\n   189\t        else:\n   190\t            if len(outs) == 1:\n   191\t                a2['outcome'] = outs[0]\n   192\t            else:\n   193\t                errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: {len(outs)} figures are marked as its outcome; exactly one is required'))\n   194\t            if len(refs) == 1 and not reason:\n   195\t                a2['reference'] = {'figure': refs[0]}\n   196\t            elif not refs and reason:\n   197\t                a2['reference'] = {'unavailable': reason}\n   198\t            else:\n   199\t                errors.append(('S5', f'{v}: needs exactly one of a figure marked as its reference or reference_unavailable'))\n   200\t        answers.append(a2)\n   201\t    for v in set(outcome_for) | set(reference_for):\n   202\t        if v not in members:\n   203\t            errors.append(('S7', f'{v} is marked on a figure but is not a member of the family'))\n   204\t    return {'figures': figures, 'answers': answers, 'decode_errors': errors}\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\t# ---------- arithmetic ----------\n   208\tdef _result_unit(op, units):\n   209\t    if any(u not in UNITS for u in units):\n   210\t        return None\n   211\t    if op in ('sum', 'difference'):\n   212\t        return units[0] if len(set(units)) == 1 else None\n   772\t        if engine.interval(f['id']) is None and not any(e[1].startswith(f['id'] + ':') for e in errors):\n   773\t            errors.append(('S2', f'{f[\"id\"]}: the value cannot be evaluated'))\n   774\t    if errors:\n   775\t        return {'errors': errors, 'recorded': [], 'published': {}}\n   776\t    answer_errors, outcomes = _answers(family, figs, engine, calc['answers'])\n   777\t    errors = answer_errors + _shared(family, figs, outcomes) + _part_whole(family, figs, engine, outcomes) + _sums(family, figs)\n   778\t    published = {v: list(engine.interval(o)) + [None] for v, o in outcomes.items()}\n   779\t    return {'errors': errors, 'recorded': _recorded(family, figs, outcomes), 'published': published}\n   780\t\n   781\t\n   782\tdef publish_decision(family, calc, result):\n   783\t    \"\"\"'refused' when a check fails; 'held' when a member is unresolved and a declared relation joins it to another member; else\n   784\t    'publish' (an unresolved member is shown as unresolved).\"\"\"\n   785\t    if result['errors']:\n   786\t        return 'refused'\n   787\t    unresolved = {a['view_id'] for a in calc['answers'] if a.get('shape') == 'unresolved'}\n   788\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   789\t        ends = {rel.get('part'), rel.get('whole'), rel.get('later'), rel.get('earlier')} - {None}\n   790\t        if ends & unresolved and ends - unresolved:\n   791\t            return 'held'\n   792\t    return 'publish'\n     1\t\"\"\"Render one stored family's judging-v13 request (old-2 calls 8729 and 8737 on 2026-09-20) and check a conforming answer through the\n     2\tv13 schema (model.check_schema) and calc_check. Harness-only, $0, no model call. Usage: python3 render_v13.py [out-prefix]\"\"\"\n     3\timport json\n     4\timport sqlite3\n     5\timport sys\n     6\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     7\t\n     8\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n     9\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    10\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    11\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    12\timport calc_check as cc  # noqa: E402\n    13\timport calc_small  # noqa: E402\n    14\timport gate  # noqa: E402\n    15\tfrom hivemind import model  # noqa: E402\n    16\t\n    17\tS, N = {'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'number'}\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\tdef nullable(schema):\n    21\t    return {'anyOf': [schema, {'type': 'null'}]}\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\tdef obj(props, desc=None):\n    25\t    out = {'type': 'object', 'properties': props, 'required': list(props), 'additionalProperties': False}\n    26\t    if desc:\n    27\t        out['description'] = desc\n    28\t    return out\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tdef v13_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\n    32\t    what = obj({k: S for k in ('population', 'measure', 'scope', 'period')},\n    33\t               'What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue or units; never its basis), scope, period.')\n    34\t    figure = obj({\n    35\t        'id': S, 'what': what,\n    36\t        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.BASES - {'prior_forecast'}), 'description': 'reported: an actual; guidance: the company\\'s '\n    37\t                  'outlook; consensus: analysts\\' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family\\'s forecast.'},\n    38\t        'scenario': S,\n    39\t        'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['computed', 'estimate', 'source'], 'description': 'source: stated in a shown passage; computed: one '\n    40\t                 'operation on named figures; estimate: your judgement, stated as yours.'},\n    41\t        'value': nullable(N), 'low': nullable(N), 'high': nullable(N),\n    42\t        'bound': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['>', '>=', '<', '<=', 'approx', 'approx_below', 'approx_above']}),\n    43\t        'unit': S,\n    44\t        'evidence': nullable(S),\n    45\t        'expression': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Source only: the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes '\n    46\t                                'it, qualifiers included (for example \"more than $2 billion\", \"$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%\", \"more than triple\").'}),\n    47\t        'component': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['value', 'bound', 'midpoint', 'relative', 'low', 'high', 'multiplier']}),\n    48\t        'inputs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    49\t        'operation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.OPERATIONS)}),\n    50\t        'signs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': N}),\n    51\t        'relation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['time_aggregation', 'accounting_parts', 'stated_in_addition', 'overlap_unknown'],\n    52\t                              'description': 'Sum and roll_forward: periods of one quantity; declared parts of a whole; a source says they add; '\n    53\t                              'unknown overlap (name the disputed figure).'}),\n    54\t        'disputed': nullable(S),\n    55\t        'bridge': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, '\n    56\t                            'declared parts, a balance and its flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an '\n    57\t                            'estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it converts.'}),\n    58\t        'basis_text': nullable(S), 'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    59\t        'adjusts': nullable(obj({'figure': S, 'type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['discount', 'uplift', 'trim']}})),\n    60\t        'converts': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    61\t    })\n    62\t    push = obj({'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    63\t    theme_push = obj({'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': theme_ids or ['none']},\n    64\t                      'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    65\t    answer = obj({\n    66\t        'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids},\n    67\t        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\n    68\t        'outcome': nullable(S), 'rung': nullable({'type': 'integer'}),\n    69\t        'reference': nullable(obj({'figure': nullable(S), 'unavailable': nullable(S)}, 'An external figure, or a calculation from external '\n    70\t                              'and reported figures, or unavailable with why.')),\n    71\t        'reasons': S, 'why': nullable(S),\n    72\t        'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}},\n    73\t        'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': push}, 'theme_pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': theme_push},\n    74\t    })\n    75\t    return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure}, 'answers': {'type': 'array', 'items': answer}})\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\tQUALIFIERS = list(calc_small.QUALIFIERS)                 # one owner: the checker's closed list\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\tdef v13s_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\n    82\t    \"\"\"The small format (SMALL-DESIGN.md §3 [52], D737, D738): each rule the checks enforce stated beside its field.\"\"\"\n    83\t    members = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids}}\n    84\t    what = obj({'population': S,\n    85\t                'measure': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The quantity, such as revenue or capital expenditure; never its basis.'},\n    86\t                'scope': S,\n    87\t                'period': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'For example FY2027, FY2027 Q3, FY2027 H1, FY2027 Q1-Q3, CY2026, end of FY2027.'}},\n    88\t               'What the number measures. Where the request lists keys (outcome keys, shared quantities), copy them exactly.')\n    89\t    figure = obj({\n    90\t        'id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Short and unique, such as F1; never a passage id.'},\n    91\t        'what': what,\n    92\t        'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['source', 'computed', 'estimate'], 'description': \"source: a number written in a shown passage's \"\n    93\t                 'quote; computed: one operation on other figures; estimate: your judgement, with its assumption in basis_text.'},\n    94\t        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['reported', 'guidance', 'consensus', 'third_party', 'forecast'], 'description': \"reported: an \"\n    95\t                  \"actual; guidance: the company's outlook; consensus: analysts' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this \"\n    96\t                  \"family's own forecast, on a computed or estimate figure only.\"},\n    97\t        'value': nullable({'type': 'number', 'description': 'A point. Give value, or low and high, never both.'}),\n    98\t        'low': nullable({'type': 'number', 'description': 'A range, low at most high, with value null.'}),\n    99\t        'high': nullable({'type': 'number', 'description': 'A range, low at most high, with value null.'}),\n   100\t        'unit': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['USD bn', '%', 'x'], 'description': 'USD bn: money in billions of US dollars ($1.2 trillion = '\n   336\tdef _same_value(a, b):\n   337\t    \"\"\"Two recomputed (interval, bound) values are the same when their bounds match and each end agrees within 1e-9 relative.\"\"\"\n   338\t    if a is None or b is None or a[1] != b[1]:\n   339\t        return False\n   340\t    return all(abs(x - y) <= 1e-9 * max(1.0, abs(x), abs(y)) for x, y in zip(a[0], b[0]))\n   341\t\n   342\t\n   343\tdef merge(parts, shared_keys, ck=cc):\n   344\t    \"\"\"Two separate answers as one calculation: each figure id prefixed by its member; then [47.1, 47c.1] a forecast of a declared\n   345\t    shared quantity in the second call is unified with the first call's forecast of the same quantity and scenario when their\n   346\t    recomputed values are the same (references point to the first, the duplicate kept beside the calculation). Duplicates inside one\n   347\t    call are never unified, and forecasts that differ are both kept, so the family's checks judge them as they judge a joint answer.\"\"\"\n   348\t    figures, answers, recomputed, owner, units = [], [], {}, {}, {}\n   349\t    for view_id, calc in parts:\n   350\t        rename = {f['id']: f'{view_id}.{f[\"id\"]}' for f in calc['figures']}\n   351\t        figs = {f['id']: f for f in calc['figures']}\n   352\t        refs = lambda f, figs=figs: list(f.get('inputs', [])) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs] + \\\n   353\t            ([f['adjusts']['figure']] if f.get('adjusts') else []) + ([f['bridge']] if f.get('bridge') else [])\n   354\t        try:\n   355\t            values = ck._evaluate_bounded(figs, refs, {})\n   356\t        except Exception:\n   357\t            values = {}\n   358\t        for f in calc['figures']:\n   359\t            g = dict(f, id=rename[f['id']])\n   360\t            for key in ('inputs', 'rests_on', 'converts'):\n   361\t                if key in g:\n   362\t                    g[key] = [rename.get(x, x) for x in g[key]]\n   363\t            for key in ('disputed', 'bridge'):\n   364\t                if key in g:\n   365\t                    g[key] = rename.get(g[key], g[key])\n   366\t            if 'adjusts' in g:\n   367\t                g['adjusts'] = dict(g['adjusts'], figure=rename.get(g['adjusts']['figure'], g['adjusts']['figure']))\n   368\t            figures.append(g)\n   369\t            recomputed[g['id']] = values.get(f['id'])\n   370\t            owner[g['id']] = view_id\n   371\t            units[g['id']] = f.get('unit')\n   372\t        for a in calc['answers']:\n   373\t            a2 = dict(a)\n   374\t            if 'outcome' in a2:\n   375\t                a2['outcome'] = rename.get(a2['outcome'], a2['outcome'])\n   376\t            if a2.get('reference', {}).get('figure'):\n   377\t                a2['reference'] = {'figure': rename.get(a2['reference']['figure'], a2['reference']['figure'])}\n   378\t            answers.append(a2)\n   379\t    key = lambda f: (f['what']['population'], f['what']['measure'], f['what']['scope'], f['what']['period'], f.get('scenario', 'base'))\n   380\t    candidates = {}\n   381\t    for g in figures:\n   382\t        if g.get('basis') == 'forecast' and ck._key(g['what']) in shared_keys:\n   383\t            candidates.setdefault(key(g), {}).setdefault(owner[g['id']], []).append(g['id'])\n   384\t    alias, duplicates = {}, []\n   385\t    for k, by_call in candidates.items():                  # [47d.2] one to one: each call holds exactly one candidate\n   386\t        if len(by_call) == 2 and all(len(ids) == 1 for ids in by_call.values()):\n   387\t            (a,), (b,) = (by_call[v] for v, _ in parts)\n   388\t            if units[a] == units[b] and _same_value(recomputed.get(a), recomputed.get(b)):   # [47b.1] equal values, [47e.2] in one unit\n   389\t                alias[b] = a\n   390\t    if alias:\n   391\t        kept = []\n   392\t        for g in figures:\n   393\t            if g['id'] in alias:\n   394\t                duplicates.append(g)\n   395\t                continue\n   396\t            for k2 in ('inputs', 'rests_on', 'converts'):\n   397\t                if k2 in g:\n   398\t                    g[k2] = [alias.get(x, x) for x in g[k2]]\n   399\t            for k2 in ('disputed', 'bridge'):\n   400\t                if k2 in g:\n   401\t                    g[k2] = alias.get(g[k2], g[k2])\n   402\t            if 'adjusts' in g:\n   403\t                g['adjusts'] = dict(g['adjusts'], figure=alias.get(g['adjusts']['figure'], g['adjusts']['figure']))\n   404\t            kept.append(g)\n   405\t        figures = kept\n   406\t        for a in answers:\n   407\t            if a.get('outcome') in alias:\n   408\t                a['outcome'] = alias[a['outcome']]\n   409\t            if a.get('reference', {}).get('figure') in alias:\n   410\t                a['reference'] = {'figure': alias[a['reference']['figure']]}\n   411\t    return {'figures': figures, 'answers': answers, 'unified': [{'kept': alias[d['id']], 'duplicate': d} for d in duplicates]}\n   412\t\n   413\t\n   414\tdef recover(out):\n     1\t\"\"\"The blind reading step of the judging-v13 paid gate (PAID-GATE.md §4): split packets.md into reader batches, list the\n     2\tdisagreements between readers A and B for a third reader, and assemble the readings file that `paid_gate.py verdict` seals.\n     3\t\n     4\tUsage:\n     5\t  python3 assemble_readings.py split <packets.md> <out folder> <batches>\n     6\t  python3 assemble_readings.py third <packets.md> <reader A json> <reader B json> <out prompt file>\n     7\t  python3 assemble_readings.py assemble <packets.md> <reader A json> <reader B json> <third json or -> <out readings json>\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\timport hashlib\n    10\timport json\n    11\timport re\n    12\timport sys\n    13\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    14\t\n    15\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    16\tQUESTIONS = ('usable', 'contradiction', 'internal_reference', 'deciding_gap')\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef sections(text):\n    20\t    \"\"\"The packets in order: [(pid, section text)], each section starting at its '## P..' line.\"\"\"\n    21\t    found = list(re.finditer(r'^## (P\\d+)\\n', text, re.M))\n    22\t    return [(m.group(1), text[m.start():(found[i + 1].start() if i + 1 < len(found) else len(text))]) for i, m in enumerate(found)]\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tdef read_json(path):\n    26\t    \"\"\"A reader's answer: the outermost JSON object in the file (fences and prose around it are ignored).\"\"\"\n    27\t    text = Path(path).read_text()\n    28\t    start, end = text.find('{'), text.rfind('}')\n    29\t    if start < 0 or end < start:\n    30\t        raise SystemExit(f'{path}: no JSON object')\n    31\t    return json.loads(text[start:end + 1])\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tdef split(packets_path, out, batches):\n    35\t    text = Path(packets_path).read_text()\n    36\t    parts = sections(text)\n    37\t    brief = (HERE / 'reader-brief-v13.md').read_text()\n    38\t    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n    39\t    size = -(-len(parts) // batches)\n    40\t    for b in range(batches):\n    41\t        chunk = parts[b * size:(b + 1) * size]\n    42\t        if chunk:\n    43\t            (out / f'batch-{b + 1}.md').write_text(brief + '\\n\\n# Packets\\n\\n' + ''.join(s for _, s in chunk))\n    44\t            print(f'batch-{b + 1}: {\", \".join(p for p, _ in chunk)} ({sum(len(s) for _, s in chunk)} chars)')\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef disagreements(a, b):\n    48\t    return sorted((pid, card, q) for pid in a for card in a[pid] for q in QUESTIONS\n    49\t                  if a[pid][card].get(q, {}).get('answer') != b.get(pid, {}).get(card, {}).get(q, {}).get('answer'))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef third(packets_path, a_path, b_path, out):\n    53\t    text = Path(packets_path).read_text()\n    54\t    by_pid = dict(sections(text))\n    55\t    a, b = read_json(a_path), read_json(b_path)\n    56\t    rows = disagreements(a, b)\n    57\t    brief = (HERE / 'reader-brief-v13.md').read_text()\n    58\t    lines = [brief, '\\n# Third reading\\n',\n    59\t             'Two readers disagreed on the questions listed below. For each one, read the packet and both readings, and give your own '\n    60\t             'answer (yes or no) with a ground naming an id of that packet. Return only JSON: '\n    61\t             '{\"P01\": {\"K1\": {\"usable\": {\"answer\": \"...\", \"ground\": \"...\"}}}} with exactly the listed packet, card and question keys.\\n']\n    62\t    for pid in sorted({r[0] for r in rows}):\n    63\t        lines.append(by_pid[pid])\n    64\t        for _, card, q in [r for r in rows if r[0] == pid]:\n    65\t            lines.append(f'Disagreement: {pid} {card} {q}\\n  Reader 1: {json.dumps(a[pid][card][q], ensure_ascii=False)}\\n'\n    66\t                         f'  Reader 2: {json.dumps(b[pid][card][q], ensure_ascii=False)}\\n')\n    67\t    Path(out).write_text('\\n'.join(lines))\n    68\t    print(f'{len(rows)} disagreements in {len({r[0] for r in rows})} packets')\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\tdef assemble(packets_path, a_path, b_path, third_path, out):\n    72\t    data = Path(packets_path).read_bytes()\n    73\t    a, b = read_json(a_path), read_json(b_path)\n    74\t    t = read_json(third_path) if third_path != '-' else {}\n    75\t    readings = {}\n    76\t    for pid in sorted(set(a) | set(b)):\n    77\t        readings[pid] = {}\n    78\t        for card in sorted(set(a.get(pid, {})) | set(b.get(pid, {}))):\n    79\t            entry = {'A': a.get(pid, {}).get(card, {}), 'B': b.get(pid, {}).get(card, {})}\n    80\t            if t.get(pid, {}).get(card):\n    81\t                entry['third'] = t[pid][card]\n    82\t            readings[pid][card] = entry\n    83\t    Path(out).write_text(json.dumps({'packets_sha256': hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), 'packets': readings}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n    84\t    print(f'{len(readings)} packets assembled; {len(disagreements(a, b))} disagreements, {sum(len(v) for v in t.values())} cards with a third reading')\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    88\t    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ''\n    89\t    if cmd == 'split' and len(sys.argv) == 5:\n    90\t        split(sys.argv[2], Path(sys.argv[3]), int(sys.argv[4]))\n    91\t    elif cmd == 'third' and len(sys.argv) == 6:\n    92\t        third(*sys.argv[2:6])\n    93\t    elif cmd == 'assemble' and len(sys.argv) == 7:\n    94\t        assemble(*sys.argv[2:7])\n    95\t    else:\n    96\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && rg -n 'paid-plan|unsupported|refus|risk|uncovered|schema|O and|S4' codex-r69b.md codex-r69.md BLIND3-RESULT.md | tail -65; nl -ba paid-mutants.log | tail -10; nl -ba round70-brief.md | head -85; ls -al ../../.. | rg 'paid_gate|\\\\.git'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && rg -n 'paid-plan|unsupported|refus|risk|uncovered|schema|O and|S4' codex-r69b.md codex-r69.md BLIND3-RESULT.md | tail -65; nl -ba paid-mutants.log | tail -10; nl -ba round70-brief.md | head -85; ls -al ../../.. | rg 'paid_gate|\\\\.git'\"","aggregated_output":"codex-r69.md:11:3. **Keep the paid test on hold, even though it can still give a meaningful result.** A complete run can pass in exactly two ways: **8 of 9** usable pairs calculated together against **at most 5** calculated separately, or **9 of 9** against **at most 6** separately. Each of the three snapshots needs at least two usable pairs calculated together. If separate calculation gets seven, even a perfect nine cannot pass. One published contradiction, one internal forecast presented as the market’s view, or one unsupported adjustment or scope change that decides the range stops a complete run on any joint or standalone answer. A standalone answer judged unusable does not by itself trigger that stop. Missing required readings or an unsent unit leave the result incomplete. [PAID-GATE.md:259](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:259) · [PAID-GATE.md:270](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:270) · [paid_gate.py:772](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:772)\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:6:- **Both adjudicators reject that mark.** The schema the writer was given says the rung is \"for a range outcome, a band it overlaps,\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:10:  schema's range clause. Both readers applied the brief as written. No earlier run had a range that crossed a rung edge, so the gap was\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:14:- **Writers:** 12 of 12 schema-valid, 12 of 12 accepted, 0 refusals, so there was no refusal review.\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:22:`schema.json`. The tally is in `TALLY.json`.\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:60:  12 with a request contradiction (run 2), to 12 of 12 with no refusal (run 3). D742's rule was followed by all six writers it applies\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:64:- **The readers did their job on substance.** They found the one reply whose decisive assumption is unsupported (R07). That is the\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:74:  - R07's unsupported share.\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:86:  - Both adjudicators rejected it. The schema the writer was given says \"'$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%' in full, given as low and high\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:108:    marked by both; K-unsupported was \"not supported\" by both.\nBLIND3-RESULT.md:112:     recorded qualifier \"none\", and both adjudicators upheld \"number misread\". But \"estimated\" is not in the qualifier list the schema\ncodex-r69b.md:5:2. **What failed.** “Claude failed five times” overstates the record. None of its five sales forecasts earned settled support, but the $42B answer split readers. Codex also invented cuts twice before giving three accepted “can’t tell” answers on the same passages. Readers still disagreed on a separate spending forecast. Luna’s behavior remains unknown. Claude is right that a completed paid run scores STOP if readers find that an unsupported adjustment decided a published standalone forecast. [BLIND6-RESULT.md:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md:40) · [BLIND7-RESULT.md:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:30) · [PAID-GATE.md:267](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:267)\ncodex-r69b.md:11:5. **How far the diagnosis reaches.** The last test located one clear failure. Repeating the same passages leaves its frequency elsewhere unknown. Question 1 settles what readers should see, and the final test shows a writer can still give them an unsupported number under that instruction. [BLIND7-RESULT.md:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:19) · [BLIND7-RESULT.md:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:30)\n    26\tCAUGHT  25 replay does not compare  FAIL  verdict: a run takes one verdict; replay reproduces it from the sealed readings, and fails once they are\n    27\tCAUGHT  26 a retry is sent before later first attempts  FAIL  every scored first attempt is sent before any retry (the provider's own call order)  10\n    28\tCAUGHT  27 completeness from the final attempts  FAIL  a diagnostic retry that fails in transport leaves the scored test complete  single-O|single|1: transport\n    29\tCAUGHT  28 the returned text is cut  FAIL  a long malformed answer is kept whole: the passage it names at its end is shown in the attempts file  e5\n    30\tCAUGHT  29 a null content is passed on  crash: TypeError: expected string or bytes-like object\n    31\tCAUGHT  30 a file is written before both render  FAIL  packets are written only after both files render: a failed render leaves nothing, and a second call then\n    32\tCAUGHT  31 records split on any line break  aborted: unicode: 36 started lines against 35 finished attempts\n    33\tCAUGHT  32 retries share the scored journal  FAIL  a damaged retry record is reported and the retry is interrupted, but the scored test stays complete  no \n    34\tCAUGHT  33 a damaged retry makes the verdict incomplete  FAIL  a damaged retry record is reported and the retry is interrupted, but the scored test stays complete  ans\n    35\t33 of 33 mutants caught; control passes\n     1\t# Council round 70 (before the paid send Alex authorized): independent review, read-only\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Context\n     6\t- **Alex's decision D753** (`docs/DECISIONS-log.md`, last entry): \"破例一次，付费重发\". This is a one-time exception to D749's\n     7\t  clean-pass condition: the 36 requests rebuilt in v13s with the D751 request, under D725's lines and `PAID-GATE.md` §4, with a total\n     8\t  cap of $0.50 including retries. It also sets \"can't tell yet\" as the E-type default, with no request change.\n     9\t- **What is ready.** Nothing has been sent.\n    10\t  - The plan: `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.json`, pinned in `paid-plan-v13s.sha256` (`0dc7c310…`). It\n    11\t    holds 12 requests × 3 draws, built by `paid_gate.py plan-v13s`. Its system text is the registered D751 request (`080a0012…`).\n    12\t  - **The code change**, in `paid_gate.py`:\n    13\t    - the constants `PINNED_PLAN_V13S` and `AUTH_V13S` (a fresh one-time key path `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/`);\n    14\t    - `send()` now picks the pin and the authorization by the plan's format and refuses a mixed plan;\n    15\t    - the v13 pin and the spent v13 authorization are unchanged.\n    16\t  - **$0 checks**, with a stub gate and scratch key paths:\n    17\t    - an altered plan is refused, and a wrong ceiling is refused;\n    18\t    - the pinned plan passes;\n    19\t    - a second use of the authorization is refused, and the old v13 plan is refused because its authorization is spent.\n    20\t    - The rehearsal passes 19 of 19, and the paid mutants are 33 of 33 caught with the control passing.\n    21\t- **The intended launch.**\n    22\t  - `python3 paid_gate.py send poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 0.5 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.json`,\n    23\t    detached, with a log and a pid file.\n    24\t  - After it: `packets`, two blind readers per packet (Codex and Claude), a third Codex reader on disagreements, then `verdict` as\n    25\t    `PAID-GATE.md` §4 registers it.\n    26\t- **The reading rule** was fixed before any answer existed (`PAID-GATE.md` §4; D731). Since then:\n    27\t  - Alex ruled D747: an explained related figure counts as support;\n    28\t  - D753 makes \"can't tell yet\" the E-type default;\n    29\t  - the free tests' reader definitions are in `blind_rules.py`.\n    30\t\n    31\t## Questions\n    32\t1. **Is the send ready?** Check:\n    33\t   - the plan's contents against the registered cases (`PAID-GATE.md`, `paid_gate.py` PAIRS and SINGLETONS);\n    34\t   - the pin, the cap and the authorization logic in `send()`;\n    35\t   - the retry policy (first attempt scored, retries diagnostic, inside the cap);\n    36\t   - that nothing else changed in the gate.\n    37\t2. **The reading rule.** Should the paid readers' brief (the `packets` text in `paid_gate.py`) carry Alex's D747 definition of\n    38\t   support, and the D753 default, before any answer exists? Or must the registered §4 rule stay exactly as fixed? What is the smallest\n    39\t   correct course that neither changes the verdict lines nor ignores Alex's later rulings?\n    40\t3. **Anything that could waste the send.** Examples: an INCOMPLETE risk, a known refusal class, a guard that would stop it for a\n    41\t   reason unrelated to luna. What does the cheaper check leave uncovered?\n    42\t4. **Verdict:** send as is, send with listed changes, or do not send.\n    43\t\n    44\tReturn a numbered report: findings marked serious / minor / wording, with citations, then the verdict.\ndrwxr-xr-x@  16 lchingen  staff    512 Nov 22 20:24 .git\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   3265 Nov 17 20:44 .gitignore\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
