last')] figures as written 3 displayed 0\npaid vs proxy same evidence False paid question What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?\nS dict_keys(['unit', 'arm', 'draw_store', 'members', 'format', 'system', 'user', 'schema', 'family', 'passages', 'evidence_ids', 'questions', 'shown'])\nclaude forecast omitted named passages 0 [] missing non-neutral [] figures as written 21 displayed 14\npaid vs proxy same evidence False paid question How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\ncodex forecast omitted named passages 0 [] missing non-neutral [] figures as written 5 displayed 5\npaid vs proxy same evidence False paid question How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\nP-v8 dict_keys(['unit', 'arm', 'draw_store', 'members', 'format', 'system', 'user', 'schema', 'family', 'passages', 'evidence_ids', 'questions', 'shown'])\nclaude forecast omitted named passages 0 [] missing non-neutral [] figures as written 12 displayed 12\ncodex forecast omitted named passages 0 [] missing non-neutral [] figures as written 12 displayed 12\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'e4764|e540[124]|e5399|\\\"reasons\\\"|\\\"why\\\"' poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json | tail -18; cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '272,285p'; ls -l /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/*/scratchpad | rg -i 'd753|r70' | tail -24; rg -n 'guard|guardrail|refus|models|known' BLIND7-RESULT.md codex-r69.md | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'e4764|e540[124]|e5399|\\\"reasons\\\"|\\\"why\\\"' poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json | tail -18; cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '272,285p'; ls -l /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/*/scratchpad | rg -i 'd753|r70' | tail -24; rg -n 'guard|guardrail|refus|models|known' BLIND7-RESULT.md codex-r69.md | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"82:      \"reasons\": \"NVIDIA's doubling outlook puts the reference at $40 billion, the lower edge of rung 2. Kress described growth as more than doubling, without sizing the excess. The FY2027 base is itself a target. Broad planned deployments and Anthropic's evaluation make an on-time ramp plausible. The stronger calendar 2027 hyperscaler spending outlook also gives those customers room to buy. Yet a major customer can deploy Vera in a small initial order or across many systems, with very different revenue in FY2028. AMD's agentic-workload tests give buyers a concrete reason to consider EPYC, but disclose no customer switching an order or negotiating a lower Vera price. Industry growth and Arm server adoption likewise give no Vera-specific order volume. Together these observations support demand and identify competitive risk, but do not favor either side of $40 billion.\",\n83:      \"why\": \"The decisive unknown is how many Vera CPUs customers will take during FY2028 and at what realized price. There is no booked volume, delivery schedule, or reported sales pace to size the gap between evaluations and revenue. Taking the target in full and discounting it into rung 3 would each require an unsupported assumption about that gap.\",\n91:        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4764\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n95:        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5399\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n97:        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5401\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n98:        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5402\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n100:        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5404\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}\n   272\t\n   273\t\n   274\tATTEMPT_FIELDS = ('attempt', 'status', 'decision', 'errors', 'data', 'raw')\n   275\t\n   276\t\n   277\tdef first_attempt(entry):\n   278\t    \"\"\"[47e.1] The attempt that is scored: the first one, on both arms (a retry is diagnostic). No attempt: not sent.\"\"\"\n   279\t    attempts = sorted(entry.get('attempts') or [], key=lambda a: a['attempt'])\n   280\t    return attempts[0] if attempts else {'attempt': 1, 'status': 'not sent', 'decision': 'not sent'}\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\tdef derive_finals(out, items, damaged=None):\n   284\t    \"\"\"Each planned unit and draw: 'dispatched' (a started line), 'completed' (a finished line), and the decision of its last finished\n   285\t    attempt (a second refusal is unresolved). A unit with no started line is not sent; one started but not finished is interrupted.\"\"\"\ndrwxr-xr-x@  36 lchingen  wheel      1152 Nov 23 02:03 paid-mutants-d753\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 lchingen  wheel       224 Nov 23 02:02 rehearsal-d753\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && python3 -B -c 'import json,paid_gate as g; from collections import Counter; plan=json.loads((g.HERE/\\\"paid-plan-v13s.json\\\").read_text()); d=g.REPO/\\\"poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E\\\"; it=json.loads((d/\\\"item.json\\\").read_text()); ii=plan[-1]; print(\\\"E evidence difference\\\",set(it[\\\"shown\\\"])-set(ii[\\\"shown\\\"]),set(ii[\\\"shown\\\"])-set(it[\\\"shown\\\"])); print(\\\"schema equality\\\",ii[\\\"schema\\\"]==it[\\\"schema\\\"],\\\"question\\\",ii[\\\"questions\\\"]==it[\\\"questions\\\"]); data=json.loads((d/\\\"answers/codex.json\\\").read_text()); calc=g.decode(data,\\\"v13s\\\",ii[\\\"family\\\"]); c=g.cs.check(ii[\\\"family\\\"],ii[\\\"passages\\\"],calc); print(\\\"accepted by paid schema\\\",g.model.check_schema(data,ii[\\\"schema\\\"])[:1],\\\"paid calc\\\",c[\\\"errors\\\"][:3]); print(\\\"D751 all replay are fully present?\\\"); print(ii[\\\"passages\\\"].get(\\\"e5399\\\")); print(\\\"current paid state: fresh key/out\\\",g.AUTH_V13S.exists(),(g.REPO/\\\"poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23\\\").exists(),\\\"old key\\\",g.AUTH.exists())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
