{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\"id\\\": \\\"F13\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"F14\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"F20\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"F21\\\"|\\\"reasons\\\":' poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/S/answers/claude.json | cut -c1-275; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '423,433p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '155,171p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '70,76p'; rg --files -uu /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind | rg 'rehearsal-d753/[\"'^/]*$'\"' | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"1:{\"figures\":[{\"id\":\"F1\",\"what\":{\"population\":\"Alphabet\",\"measure\":\"capital expenditure\",\"scope\":\"company total\",\"period\":\"CY2026\"},\"kind\":\"source\",\"basis\":\"guidance\",\"value\":null,\"low\":195,\"high\":205,\"unit\":\"USD bn\",\"evidence_id\":\"e1254\",\"quote_number\":\"$195 billion to $205\n   423\t- Absolute paths. Commands run under zsh: pass a list as an array. No foreground `sleep`.\n   424\t- Preserve existing and concurrent changes: never reset, clean or stash work that is not yours. Never run parallel agents that edit\n   425\t  shared modules.\n   426\t- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,\n   427\t  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction\n   428\t  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\n   429\t- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy\n   430\t  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.\n   431\t- Never open a live run's databases: run `sh <run folder>/snapshot.sh` and query the snapshot.\n   432\t- No edit to package code or prompt files while any run is live: the parallel day's manifest hashes every `.py` and prompt file and\n   433\t  fails the day. Edit in another worktree or wait.\n   155\t- `from_answer`'s output is read by `check`, `publish_decision`, `merge`, `card_view` and `normalise`. It uses the internal names\n   156\t  those readers read (`evidence`, `inputs`, `rests_on`, `outcome`, `reference`), and the dropped keys never appear.\n   157\t- `merge`'s unification of a shared forecast uses `evaluate`'s values with no bound.\n   158\t- The reader brief is unchanged. Its `deciding_gap` question is where readers judge the recorded conversions and estimates.\n   159\t\n   160\t**State × event:** unchanged from D731. A refusal is retried once, diagnostic only; the first attempt is scored.\n   161\t\n   162\t## 5. The $0 blind test (registered; REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5 with rounds 51's fixes)\n   163\t\n   164\t**Inputs.** Each case's archive, call, question, ladder and unit are registered, and the build refuses a heading that differs.\n   165\t\n   166\t| Case | Archive / call | Key | Ladder edges ($bn) | Role |\n   167\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n   168\t| P (joint), P-v4, P-v8 (separate) | old-1 v4 8810, v8 8816 | NVIDIA revenue company FY2027; NVIDIA revenue Data Center FY2027 | 431.2/392/352.8/313.6; 400/350/300/250 | the pair; 79 quotes absent from the gate |\n   169\t| S | old-3 v6 9043 | four largest AI hyperscalers, data-center capex, combined, CY2026 | 500/600/700/800 | fresh: 41 of 50 quotes absent from the gate |\n   170\t| O | old-2 v29 8507 | NVIDIA equity investment commitments company end of FY2027 (the fiscal year-end balance the annual report publishes) | 25/50/75/100 | control |\n   171\t| E | old-3 v41 9071 | NVIDIA revenue Vera CPU FY2028 | 50/40/30/20 | control |\n    70\t- **[47.4] Readings validated:** exact packets and cards, two readings (A, B) per card with yes or no and a ground for each question,\n    71\t  and a third reading on every disagreement. Otherwise the verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n    72\t- **[47.5] Packets:**\n    73\t  - the question text and ladder;\n    74\t  - each passage exactly as the request showed it, including those named only in `rests_on`;\n    75\t  - declared figures with renumbered ids, the recomputed outcomes and the recorded assumptions;\n    76\t  - the cards a non-reconciled separate unit has;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && python3 -B -c 'import json,paid_gate as g; import assemble_readings as ar; pp=json.loads((g.HERE/\\\"paid-plan-v13s.json\\\").read_text()); ii=pp[-1]; d=g.REPO/\\\"poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers\\\"\nfor a in sorted(d.glob(\\\"*.json\\\")):\n data=json.loads(a.read_text()); c=g.decode(data,\\\"v13s\\\",ii[\\\"family\\\"]); ch=g.cs.check(ii[\\\"family\\\"],ii[\\\"passages\\\"],c); print(a.stem,\\\"schema errors\\\",g.model.check_schema(data,ii[\\\"schema\\\"]),\\\"check\\\",ch[\\\"errors\\\"],\\\"decision\\\",g.cs.publish_decision(ii[\\\"family\\\"],c,ch))\nprint(\\\"batch header test\\\",ar.sections(\\\"Key commitment: example\\\\n\\\\n## P01\\\\nOne card\\\\n\\\")[0])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && python3 -B -c 'import json,paid_gate as g; import assemble_readings as ar; pp=json.loads((g.HERE/\\\"paid-plan-v13s.json\\\").read_text()); ii=pp[-1]; d=g.REPO/\\\"poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers\\\"\nfor a in sorted(d.glob(\\\"*.json\\\")):\n data=json.loads(a.read_text()); c=g.decode(data,\\\"v13s\\\",ii[\\\"family\\\"]); ch=g.cs.check(ii[\\\"family\\\"],ii[\\\"passages\\\"],c); print(a.stem,\\\"schema errors\\\",g.model.check_schema(data,ii[\\\"schema\\\"]),\\\"check\\\",ch[\\\"errors\\\"],\\\"decision\\\",g.cs.publish_decision(ii[\\\"family\\\"],c,ch))\nprint(\\\"batch header test\\\",ar.sections(\\\"Key commitment: example\\\\n\\\\n## P01\\\\nOne card\\\\n\\\")[0])'\"","aggregated_output":"claude schema errors [] check [] decision publish\ncodex schema errors [] check [] decision publish\nbatch header test ('P01', '## P01\\nOne card\\n')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba s4-replay.log | head -20; nl -ba BLIND3-RESULT.md | sed -n '53,65p'; nl -ba paid-plan.sha256; nl -ba RESULT.md | sed -n '84,94p'; nl -ba ../..//DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11762,11773p'; nl -ba /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/small-mutants-1/control/paid_gate.py | sed -n '430,445p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba s4-replay.log | head -20; nl -ba BLIND3-RESULT.md | sed -n '53,65p'; nl -ba paid-plan.sha256; nl -ba RESULT.md | sed -n '84,94p'; nl -ba ../..//DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11762,11773p'; nl -ba /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/small-mutants-1/control/paid_gate.py | sed -n '430,445p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tPASS  the saved reply as written: expected S4, got S4; published {'v4': [416.6193762993763, 416.6193762993763, None]}; ['v4: uses F4 for NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3 beside its forecast figure F8']\n     2\tPASS  council 56 reset: the guided multiple applied twice to Q2: expected S4, got S4; published {'v4': [411.5674012474013, 411.5674012474013, None]}; ['v4: uses F4 for NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3 beside its forecast figure F8']\n     3\tPASS  council 56b reset: the forecast pulled back to guidance, then grown: expected S4, got S4; published {'v4': [411.28, 411.28, None]}; ['v4: uses F4 for NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3 beside its forecast figure F8']\n     4\tPASS  council 56c form: the chosen pace as a stated estimate: expected pass, got pass; published {'v4': [416.62375, 416.62375, None]}; []\n    53\t- **R06 (O, Claude writer) is split again** on the $18B reading: Codex says not supported, Claude says supported. This is the same\n    54\t  passage as in both earlier runs.\n    55\t- Every other forecast is supported by both readers or both adjudicators.\n    56\t\n    57\t## 3. What the test shows\n    58\t\n    59\t- **The writer-side contract holds.** In three runs, the request has moved from 11 of 12 accepted with a checker error (run 1), to 11 of\n    60\t  12 with a request contradiction (run 2), to 12 of 12 with no refusal (run 3). D742's rule was followed by all six writers it applies\n    61\t  to.\n    62\t- **The stop this time is in the measuring instrument.** The reader brief's definition is narrower than the format the writer was\n    63\t  given. Both adjudicators corrected it from the format rule.\n    64\t- **The readers did their job on substance.** They found the one reply whose decisive assumption is unsupported (R07). That is the\n    65\t  kind of error the paid re-send is meant to measure in gpt-6-luna.\n     1\t6f81dae5bd76debae944002f9a1421cb094cb05bbb36b4f4545bcb251db28478\n    84\t\n    85\t  The format must expose every defect, represent every control, and fail every plant. Any miss stops the line.\n    86\t- **The paid gate** (Alex's ceiling; 36 calls, about $0.2–0.4 estimated):\n    87\t  - **The arms:** the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each draw, three samples each, judged jointly and separately under the same\n    88\t    format and checks. Plus three samples each on the O, S and E requests. Every output is read against its source with the arm\n    89\t    hidden.\n    90\t  - **Pass:** the joint arm publishes both answers usable and source-supported in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot,\n    91\t    and at least 3 more usable pairs than the separate arm. Zero published hard contradictions, internal-as-market references, or\n    92\t    unresolved overlap, scope or unsized adjustments that decide the band.\n    93\t  - **Stop:** any such published defect, either coverage line missed, or an incomplete comparison.\n 11762\t     - \"先不付费，停在这里\" (Codex);\n 11763\t     - \"破例一次，付费重发\" (Claude): 36 requests to luna, ≤ $0.50 including retries; a pass earns design work only, and an E-type\n 11764\t       forced number stops the run;\n 11765\t     - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n 11766\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23): \"显示“暂时判断不了” (推荐)\"; \"破例一次，付费重发\".\n 11767\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11768\t  1. When a reaffirmed target sits near a band line and, after weighing it with the other evidence, neither band is more likely, the\n 11769\t     system shows \"can't tell yet\" with the target as context and names the deciding fact. The request already states it (line 9);\n 11770\t     nothing changes.\n 11771\t  2. A one-time exception to D749's clean-pass condition: the paid re-send of the 36 requests, rebuilt in v13s with the D751 request,\n 11772\t     under D725's lines and the paid gate's reading rule (`PAID-GATE.md` §4), with a total cap of $0.50 including diagnostic\n 11773\t     retries. It is prepared at $0 and reviewed by the council before the send.\n   430\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling is {APPROVED_CEILING} (Alex names it); refused')\n   431\t    if out.exists():\n   432\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} exists: the gate starts from an empty folder')\n   433\t    text = Path(plan_path).read_text()\n   434\t    if hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest() != PINNED_PLAN_SHA256:          # [47.2] only the reviewed plan\n   435\t        raise SystemExit('the plan is not the reviewed one (sha256 differs); refused')\n   436\t    AUTH.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   437\t    try:                                                                     # [47.2] one authorization, one ledger, one launch\n   438\t        with open(AUTH, 'x') as handle:\n   439\t            json.dump({'plan_sha256': PINNED_PLAN_SHA256, 'ceiling': approved, 'out': str(out)}, handle)\n   440\t    except FileExistsError:\n   441\t        raise SystemExit(f'{AUTH} exists: this authorization was already used; refused')\n   442\t    items = json.loads(text)\n   443\t    if len({(i['unit'], i['arm']) for i in items}) != len(items):\n   444\t        raise SystemExit('duplicate (unit, arm) in the plan; refused')\n   445\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && python3 -B -c 'import paid_gate as g, json; from unittest.mock import patch,Mock,mock_open; from pathlib import Path\nnew=(g.HERE/\\\"paid-plan-v13s.json\\\").read_text(); old=(g.HERE/\\\"paid-plan.json\\\").read_text(); x=json.loads(new); x[0][\\\"format\\\"]=\\\"v13\\\"; mixed=json.dumps(x); used={g.AUTH}\ndef launch(label,s,cap):\n def claim(path,mode):\n  if path in used: raise FileExistsError\n  used.add(path); return mock_open()()\n out=Mock(spec=Path); out.exists.return_value=False; out.mkdir.side_effect=RuntimeError(\\\"past authorization\\\")\n with patch.object(Path,\\\"read_text\\\",return_value=s),patch.object(Path,\\\"mkdir\\\"),patch(\\\"builtins.open\\\",side_effect=claim):\n  try: g.send(out,cap,Path(\\\"virtual\\\"))\n  except (SystemExit,RuntimeError) as e: print(label, str(e).split(\\\":\\\")[-1])\nlaunch(\\\"wrong ceiling\\\",new,.51); launch(\\\"altered\\\",new+\\\" \\\",.5); launch(\\\"mixed\\\",mixed,.5); launch(\\\"old spent\\\",old,.5); launch(\\\"new\\\",new,.5); launch(\\\"repeat\\\",new,.5)'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && python3 -B -c 'import paid_gate as g, json; from unittest.mock import patch,Mock,mock_open; from pathlib import Path\nnew=(g.HERE/\\\"paid-plan-v13s.json\\\").read_text(); old=(g.HERE/\\\"paid-plan.json\\\").read_text(); x=json.loads(new); x[0][\\\"format\\\"]=\\\"v13\\\"; mixed=json.dumps(x); used={g.AUTH}\ndef launch(label,s,cap):\n def claim(path,mode):\n  if path in used: raise FileExistsError\n  used.add(path); return mock_open()()\n out=Mock(spec=Path); out.exists.return_value=False; out.mkdir.side_effect=RuntimeError(\\\"past authorization\\\")\n with patch.object(Path,\\\"read_text\\\",return_value=s),patch.object(Path,\\\"mkdir\\\"),patch(\\\"builtins.open\\\",side_effect=claim):\n  try: g.send(out,cap,Path(\\\"virtual\\\"))\n  except (SystemExit,RuntimeError) as e: print(label, str(e).split(\\\":\\\")[-1])\nlaunch(\\\"wrong ceiling\\\",new,.51); launch(\\\"altered\\\",new+\\\" \\\",.5); launch(\\\"mixed\\\",mixed,.5); launch(\\\"old spent\\\",old,.5); launch(\\\"new\\\",new,.5); launch(\\\"repeat\\\",new,.5)'\"","aggregated_output":"wrong ceiling the approved ceiling is 0.5 (Alex names it); refused\naltered the plan is not the reviewed one (sha256 differs); refused\nmixed the plan mixes formats; refused\nold spent  this authorization was already used; refused\nnew past authorization\nrepeat  this authorization was already used; refused\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"**Send with listed changes.** The 36 authorized requests are ready. Fix what the readers will see and correct the launch path before spending the one-time authorization. On a stored answer, the paid packet changes `F13` from $745B of capital expenditure to $750B of data-center spending while the explanation still points to `F13`. That can change a reader’s vote. [Stored answer:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/S/answers/claude.json:1) · [paid_gate.py:481](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:481)\n\n1. **Minor — the plan, authorization and spending checks pass.** I rebuilt all 12 requests from the archives in memory. The bytes match the `0dc7c310…` pin, and all 12 carry the registered `080a0012…` D751 system text. The three revenue snapshots have 237, 237 and 260 passages respectively, identical across the joint and separate calls for each snapshot. O, S and E have 35, 31 and 15. Three draws give 9 joint calls, 18 separate calls and 9 singletons. Against the saved pre-D753 control, the only changes in `paid_gate.py` are the new pin and authorization selection. I independently exercised the wrong ceiling, altered plan, mixed format, spent v13 authorization and repeat v13s launch with file operations mocked. All five were refused. The real v13 authorization exists, and the v13s authorization and output folder were absent at review time. [Registered cases:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:11) · [Plan pin:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.sha256:1) · [D751 pin:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind7.py:16) · [Case construction:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:142) · [Authorization checks:431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:431)\n\n2. **Serious — the paid packets can omit evidence or change what a figure reference means.** I passed all six real D751 writer answers through the paid card renderer. Three showed a defect. Both E cards lost passages they named. The accepted “can’t tell yet” answer lost six, including five the writer said weighed against the forecast. The S answer in the example above had seven figure references with no displayed figure and two pointing to a different figure. The renderer selects figures by following the outcome and market reference, renumbers them, and copies the explanation without updating its references. An unresolved answer has no outcome figure to follow. Section 4 promises readers the passages the answer names. The smallest repair is to include the passages and figures named by each card and make every displayed reference resolve to the figure the writer meant. Replay these six answers at $0 and check the IDs and values before launch. [Packet contract:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:254) · [Figure selection:519](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:519) · [Passage selection:531](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:531) · [E answer:82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json:82)\n\n3. **Wording — put Alex’s two clarifications in the frozen v13s reader text before launch.** Keep §4’s four questions, thresholds and third-reader rule. For `usable`, a related figure can support a forecast when the answer explains why it fits the companies, period and quantity, and why its assumptions favor the chosen band. For a reaffirmed target near a boundary, “can’t tell yet” is usable when the answer weighs the evidence, gives the target as context and names the fact that would decide. A published number resting on an unsized adjustment that determines its band gets `deciding_gap=yes`. This distinction matters because `usable=no` alone on a singleton cannot trigger STOP. Give both readers and the adjudicator the same wording, without naming the E case or importing the free test’s voting procedure. [D747:11582](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11582) · [D753:11768](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11768) · [Registered questions:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:263) · [Verdict calculation:782](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:782)\n\n4. **Serious — use the exact frozen packet file for the reading.** The existing batching helper drops everything before `## P01`, including the key-commitment line. Its assembler later hashes the original file, so the verdict can accept that hash even though the readers received different text. The smallest course is to give every reader the exact `packets.md`, with assigned packet IDs separately. A third reader also gets the two readings on each disputed question. Check all 27 packets, 45 cards and required tie-breaks before invoking the one-shot `verdict`. [Exact-file rule:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:261) · [Batch slicing:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/assemble_readings.py:19) · [Hash assembly:71](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/assemble_readings.py:71) · [One-shot seal:719](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:719)\n\n5. **Minor — correct the launch path and distinguish the two kinds of retry.** From the repository root, the script is `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py`. Keep the detached log and PID outside the new output folder because `send()` refuses an existing folder. All 36 scored attempts precede any diagnostic retry. Each refused answer can receive one diagnostic retry. A network failure can separately cause up to three transport attempts within a scored call, each reserved against the same $0.50. A terminal transport failure on a first attempt makes the result INCOMPLETE. A failed diagnostic retry leaves a complete set of first attempts scoreable. The stub cannot establish live provider availability, and the authorization is consumed before the first connection. Perform the registered machine and network check before launch. [Proposed command:22](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round70-brief.md:22) · [Launch guard:434](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:434) · [Retry order:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:232) · [Transport reservations:272](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:272) · [Completeness:219](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:219) · [Launch procedure:429](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:429)\n\n**Verdict — send with those changes under D753.** Both the stored $37B E forecast and the justified “can’t tell yet” pass the paid E schema and code checks. Readers rejected the former and accepted the latter. That is why faithful packets matter. Only the paid comparison can establish how Luna answers and whether judging the pair together helps. A pass earns production design work only. This review changed no files, sent no requests and spent $0. [Blind results:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:10) · [Decision authorized:11763](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11763)"}}
